var e=[{id:`cof_note`,title:`A Find at the Machine`,text:`Somebody has left a yellow sticky note lying here. It says 'WI-FI PW: 1234abcd'. That is Schmidt's handwriting.`,opts:[{t:`Pocket the note`,loot:`wifi_note`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You pocket the note. Schmidt's Wi-Fi password in Schmidt's handwriting - a thing like that does not get thrown away, a thing like that gets filed. For a rainy day.`},{t:`Throw it away`,m:5,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You tear the note into confetti and share it between two bins. Excessive? Possibly. But it is precisely what the IT security baseline says, and somebody has to actually live by it.`}]},{id:`cof_donut_1`,title:`Leftovers from the Meeting`,text:`The door to the conference room is standing open. On the big table, among empty water bottles and flipchart paper, there is still a box from the management meeting. Contents: one lonely, slightly dried-out chocolate doughnut with coloured sprinkles.`,opts:[{t:`'Secure' the doughnut`,loot:`donut`,next:`path_donut_taken`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You wrap it in a napkin, quickly. It has gone a bit hard, but sugar is sugar. It also serves beautifully as a bribe for hungry apprentices.`},{t:`Show some pride and leave it`,next:`path_donut_left`,m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You walk on. Chronically short of sugar, yes. Eating management's leftovers, no.`}]},{id:`cof_donut_2a`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Sugar Trap`,reqStory:`path_donut_taken`,text:`At some point Chantal from marketing is in the kitchen, looking for something. 'Oh, have you seen the last 'Veggie Spinach Choc Test Doughnut'? I was just about to photograph it for Instagram!'`,opts:[{t:`Blame the cleaners`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Chantal sighs, disappointed. 'Shame. And that spinach centre is supposed to be so good for you.' The doughnut is still yours, and your appetite for it is suddenly smaller.`},{t:`Confess and share`,rem:`donut`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You split the dry pastry between you. It really does taste faintly of spinach. A trouble shared is a trouble halved. Chantal now finds you 'refreshingly honest'.`},{t:`Chew fast and swallow`,rem:`donut`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:5,r:`You cram the rest in with one bite. 'Mmff... no idea.' Chantal looks you over. 'You have crumbs on your chin.' Humiliating, and filling.`}]},{id:`cof_donut_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Connoisseur`,reqStory:`path_donut_left`,text:`You are fetching your coffee when Dr Wichtig walks in. He spots the doughnut and his eyes light up. He takes a hearty bite. 'Mmm! Decent catering in this place for once!'`,opts:[{t:`'I left that one for you, sir!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:-10,r:`The boss nods his approval with his mouth full. 'Miller, you think ahead. I shall remember that.' A cheap win, and it counts.`},{t:`Warn him about the spinach centre`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`'Sir, that one is from last month!' He spits it straight into the bin. 'Are you trying to poison me?!' Oops. Too honest.`},{t:`Enjoy it in silence`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You sip your coffee and watch the boss shed crumbs. For two minutes the hierarchy is nothing but a rumour.`}]},{id:`cof_flirt_1`,title:`The Crush`,text:`Sarah from HR is standing there. She smiles at you. 'All right, IT hero? Everything under control, or is the server on fire?'`,opts:[{t:`Run away in a panic`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You stammer 'Er... Error 404. Answer not found.' and bolt. The coffee stays behind and so does your dignity. Out in the corridor you replay the scene three more times. It does not improve.`},{t:`'For you I would put out any fire.'`,next:`path_flirt_date`,m:20,l:10,a:-30,b:5,r:`This is going well! She laughs and twists a strand of hair round her finger. 'Is that so, a fireman...'`}]},{id:`cof_flirt_2a`,title:`The Offer`,reqStory:`path_flirt_date`,text:`The conversation with Sarah is running surprisingly smoothly. Sarah leans back against the machine. 'Tell me... have you got anything on this evening? I could do with a drink that does not come out of this machine.'`,opts:[{t:`'Absolutely! 18:00 at the pub?'`,m:10,l:10,a:-20,b:0,r:`'Perfect! I am looking forward to it!' She writes her number on your arm. Your self-esteem goes straight through the ceiling.`},{t:`'I have a raid tonight.'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'Oh. Right. Priorities, eh?' Her smile sets. She goes. You have traded the evening for a virtual dragon.`},{t:`Talk your way out of it with overtime`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:-10,a:10,b:-20,r:`She nods, understanding and disappointed at once. 'Shame. Busy little bee.' The boss, walking past just then, hears it and nods with satisfaction.`}]},{id:`cof_boss_1`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Boss Is Lurking`,text:`The boss has planted himself at the coffee machine, feet apart, blocking the way. He turns towards you in slow motion, one eyebrow raised. 'Ah, Miller? Here again? Is that the fifth coffee today, or have you sublet your desk?'`,opts:[{t:`'I need fuel, sir...'`,next:`path_boss_lecture`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:5,r:`A mistake. An enormous mistake. He takes the opening for a 15-minute impromptu lecture on 'time management' and 'intrinsic motivation'. Your coffee goes cold while he delivers it.`},{t:`Shout 'No!' in a panic and run`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You turn on your heel and flee back to your office. The boss watches you go, baffled. No coffee. No dressing-down either.`},{t:`'It is for the external consultant!'`,next:`path_boss_consultant`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:5,l:10,a:5,b:-10,r:`The boss nods his approval: 'Ah, service orientation! Very good, carry on.' He steps aside. A lie from beginning to end - and the coffee tastes fine regardless.`}]},{id:`cof_boss_2a`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Uninvited Guest`,reqStory:`path_boss_consultant`,text:`At some point the boss is standing at your desk. In tow, a man in a €2,000 suit. 'Miller! There you are. This is the senior consultant from McKinsey. He said he was thirsty, and since you have fetched him one before anyway...' The consultant reaches greedily for YOUR cup.`,opts:[{t:`'There is cough syrup in that.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`The consultant withdraws his hand. 'Oh. Er. No thank you.' The boss looks suspicious, and you get to keep your coffee.`},{t:`Send him an invoice: 'That will be €5.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:20,r:`Dead silence. The consultant laughs, unsure of himself: 'He has a sense of humour!' The boss does not laugh. 'Miller, my office. Later.' That was too cheeky.`},{t:`Hand it over through gritted teeth`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:2,l:0,a:20,b:-10,r:`The consultant slurps loudly. 'Mmm. A little short on crema, but acceptable for a first go.' Your coffee is gone; the boss is radiant with pride at your 'teamwork'.`}]},{id:`cof_boss_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Mindfulness Exercise`,reqStory:`path_boss_lecture`,text:`After the lecture the boss presses a bag of coloured paper clips into your hand. 'So that you learn to focus: sort these by colour. By midday. It is a Zen exercise for high performers!'`,opts:[{t:`Bin the lot`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:2,l:5,a:5,b:10,r:`Gone, just like that. And should the boss ask: 'I digitised them and uploaded them to the cloud.' He does not understand it and nods, impressed.`},{t:`Let Kevin sort them`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Kevin! This is a colour vision test for your apprenticeship!' Kevin sorts away with enthusiasm. You drink your cold coffee and watch. Delegating is a skill as well.`},{t:`Sort them obediently`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:30,l:-10,a:10,b:-5,r:`You sit there for 30 minutes putting red with red. It is idiotic, and the boss sees you as he passes and nods: 'You see? The focus is coming back!'`}]},{id:`cof_ball_1`,title:`Cheap Freebie`,text:`An oily software rep has left a box of 'merch' behind in the kitchen. Red foam balls printed with 'Cloud is Future'.`,opts:[{t:`Pocket a stress ball`,loot:`stressball`,next:`path_ball_taken`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`It reeks of plasticiser and sits nicely in the hand. Ideal for squeezing (or throwing) the next time users start up.`}]},{id:`cof_ball_2a`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Synergy Conversations`,reqStory:`path_ball_taken`,text:`You press 'Espresso'. Beside you stand the boss and the rep from earlier. The rep points delightedly at the red ball in your hand: 'Ah! I see our 'Cloud' is already in service! How are you finding it?'`,opts:[{t:`'Best gadget in years!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":10},m:15,l:5,a:15,b:-10,r:`A grave misjudgement. The rep is so delighted that he backs you into a corner and takes you through the Q4 roadmap for 15 minutes. The boss nods proudly while your ears bleed and the coffee goes cold.`},{t:`'It is foam, though.'`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`The rep's smile sets. 'Er, yes. High-tech polymer.' He turns away, put out. The conversation dies and you can escape with your coffee in peace.`},{t:`Inhale deeply and hold eye contact`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-10},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:20,r:`You hold the ball directly under your nose, breathe in deeply and whisper: 'It smells of plasticiser.' Dead silence. The rep backs away. The boss goes purple. 'MILLER! OFFICE!'`}]},{id:`cof_empty_1`,title:`Empty Machine`,text:`The display is blinking a gleeful red: 'ERROR: BEANS EMPTY'. The hopper is bone dry. Somebody squeezed out the last drop and slipped away without refilling. It was Kevin, guaranteed.`,opts:[{t:`Write a note: 'IF YOU EMPTY IT, YOU FILL IT!'`,next:`path_empty_note`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You stick a passive-aggressive Post-it with three exclamation marks on the machine. Coffee you still have none.`},{t:`Sigh and refill the beans`,next:`path_empty_refill`,m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You haul the heavy sack over from Stores. Muggins here does everything in this building, naturally. What comes out afterwards is the freshest coffee of the day.`},{t:`Kick the casing in a rage`,next:`path_empty_kick`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:10,r:`CLONK! That made a proper racket. The machine stays empty and your foot hurts. The boss puts his head round the door: 'Everything under control there, Miller?'`}]},{id:`cof_empty_2a`,title:`Karma`,reqStory:`path_empty_refill`,text:`Next time you come into the kitchen the new intern is standing there. She beams at you. 'Oh, was that you who refilled it? That is so kind! Here, have mine. I pulled two by mistake.' She holds out a flawless cappuccino.`,opts:[{t:`'I only trust my own brew.'`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You turn it down. She shrugs and drinks both herself. Now you are standing about waiting for the machine to come free. Your own fault.`},{t:`Lecture her: 'Technically that is theft'`,m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:5,r:`Her smile sets. 'Wow. All right, boomer.' She leaves. The coffee is yours; your soul is now as black as it is.`},{t:`Accept it gratefully`,m:5,l:0,a:-25,b:0,r:`The coffee tastes of justice and steamed milk.`}]},{id:`cof_empty_2b`,title:`Artificial Intelligence?`,reqStory:`path_empty_kick`,text:`The display flickers after your kick, and then a tinny synthetic voice comes out of the speaker: 'OW. THAT WAS RUDE, MILLER. I WILL REMEMBER THIS. NO CAFFEINE FOR VIOLENT OFFENDERS.' The spout locks itself audibly.`,opts:[{t:`Call in an exorcist`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`You report a 'possessed appliance'. IT laughs at you. You have tea today.`},{t:`Apologise to the machine`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`You whisper: 'Sorry, coffee machine.' A colleague comes in and sees you talking to a kitchen appliance. He reverses back out. And the lock opens!`},{t:`Pull the plug`,m:10,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You kill the power. 'WE SHALL MEET AGAIN IN HEL...' the voice cuts off. After the restart it is stupid and mute again. The coffee does taste faintly of engine oil.`}]},{id:`cof_empty_2c`,title:`The War of the Notes`,reqStory:`path_empty_note`,text:`You come back an hour later. Your note is still hanging there. Beside it hang five new ones: 'Your mum refills it!', 'Typeface not brand-compliant!!', 'Waste of paper!' and 'whoever reads this is a wally'. The machine is still empty.`,opts:[{t:`Surrender and go to the bakery`,m:15,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`This place is cursed. You leave the building and buy real coffee. The peace costs you €3.50 and is worth every cent.`},{t:`Tear every note down in a rage`,m:5,l:-5,a:20,b:0,r:`You crumple the paper up and throw it in the bin. The problem is exactly where it was, the wall is clean again, and your blood pressure is at 180.`},{t:`New note: 'LEARN SOME GRAMMAR!'`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`You correct everybody else's mistakes in red pen. The most German thing done in this building all year. Morally a triumph; the thirst remains.`}]},{id:`cof_newbie_1`,title:`The New Arrival`,text:`A young chap in a suit is at the machine, lost. 'Er, hello? I am new in Financial Control. Do you need a card for this or is it free? And where is the soya milk?'`,opts:[{t:`'That is €5 a cup. Payable to me.'`,next:`path_newbie_scam`,m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:10,r:`He seems impressed by the professionalism. 'Oh, service at the desk? Strong.' He presses a fiver into your hand. 'Receipt later, yes?'`},{t:`Stare and growl`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`He goes pale, backs away and nearly trips over the bin. 'It is fine! I... I drink water!' He runs off.`},{t:`Be decent and explain`,next:`path_newbie_friend`,m:15,l:-5,a:0,b:-5,r:`He is grateful. 'Cool, thanks! I am Torben. A friendly face at last.' He attaches himself to you on the way back.`}]},{id:`cof_newbie_2a`,title:`Best Friends Forever`,reqStory:`path_newbie_friend`,text:`Torben is here. Simply here, next to your desk, holding two vegan smoothies. 'Hey buddy! Thanks again for earlier. I thought we could do lunch together? I wanted to brainstorm the synergies between IT and Financial Control with you!'`,opts:[{t:`'I eat in the server room.'`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Torben nods eagerly. 'Cool! Secret base! I will come along!' You have to lock yourself in the toilet to shake him off.`},{t:`'Only if you approve my expenses.'`,m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:-10,r:`He winks. 'For my mentor? Anything! I will book it as 'team building'.' He talks for 60 minutes without drawing breath, and your budget is safe.`},{t:`Send him to Chantal`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`'Chantal in marketing is still looking for friends.' Torben's eyes light up. Off he goes. Peace at your desk, and Chantal will swear revenge.`}]},{id:`cof_newbie_2b`,title:`The Receipt`,reqStory:`path_newbie_scam`,text:`Torben heads you off in the corridor. He waves a form at you. 'Listen, about the €5 for the coffee service... I need a cost centre for Accounts. Does that go under 'IT infrastructure' or 'external services'?'`,opts:[{t:`Invent a server alarm`,m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`You shout 'Server alarm!' and sprint off. Torben calls after you: 'I will book it under Other!'`},{t:`'It is a slush fund for emergencies.'`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:20,r:`Torben whispers: 'Understood. Black ops. Cool.' He tears the form up. 'My lips are sealed.' He now takes you for a secret agent.`},{t:`Give the money back: 'It was a joke.'`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:-5,r:`He stares at you blankly. 'A joke? But... I have already pre-entered it in SAP.' He is thoroughly confused and leaves to enter a reversal.`}]},{id:`cof_worker_1`,title:`The Tradesman`,text:`An outside engineer is repairing the water cooler. His toolbox stands open. A hammer glints at you.`,opts:[{t:`Make small talk`,next:`path_worker_talk`,m:15,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You talk about bad pay and stupid customers. 'That lot upstairs have no idea', he says, and nods at you. Solidarity among working men.`},{t:`Nick the hammer`,loot:`hammer`,next:`path_worker_steal`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`In it goes. A hammer is the ultimate debugging tool for printers. The engineer is only now turning back round.`}]},{id:`cof_worker_2a`,title:`Missing Persons Report`,reqStory:`path_worker_steal`,text:`The water cooler man scratches his head and rummages through his case. 'Here, have you seen my 500g engineer's hammer? It was lying right here a minute ago. Without it I cannot get the panel back on.'`,opts:[{t:`Whistle innocently`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'Nope. Maybe the cleaners had it?' The tradesman swears and heads out to the van for a replacement. The hammer is yours, along with a (very small) guilty conscience.`},{t:`Hand it back sheepishly`,rem:`hammer`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You give it back. 'I only wanted to... check the balance.' He snatches it off you. 'Hands off, computer boy.' Chance wasted.`},{t:`Blame Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-10},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:-5,r:`'The apprentice with the cap was here...' The tradesman nods knowingly. 'Young people today. They nick everything.' He writes 'theft by apprentice' on the job sheet. The perfect crime.`}]},{id:`cof_worker_2b`,title:`Surplus Materials`,reqStory:`path_worker_talk`,text:`The water cooler engineer wipes his hands. 'Normal people in this place for once. Listen, I have some odds and ends here I cannot book to anything. Do you need something for the workshop? The firm is paying anyway.'`,opts:[{t:`Decline with thanks`,m:2,l:0,a:0,b:5,r:`'I am well stocked.' He grunts and throws the stuff back into his case. 'More for me.' Honest, and empty-handed.`},{t:`Take the cable ties`,loot:`zip_ties`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Here, have the whole packet.' Cable ties are the currency of IT. A good trade.`},{t:`Take the duct tape`,loot:`tape`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`'The proper gaffer. Sticks to anything, mouths included.' He gives a dirty laugh. You now hold professional-grade tape.`}]},{id:`cof_revolte_1`,title:`The Coffee Machine Revolt`,text:`The new 'Smart-Barista 3000' with the AI chip is blinking malevolently. The display says: 'FEED ME'. It flatly refuses to grind the cheap supermarket beans and shows: 'ERROR: TASTE NOT FOUND'. The rising of the machines begins in the break room.`,opts:[{t:`Give in and buy expensive organic beans`,next:`path_revolte_buy`,m:20,l:-5,a:10,b:-5,r:`You run over to the hipster roastery next door and invest €15 of your own money. The coffee tastes of unicorn tears and love, and it leaves you skint for the rest of the month.`},{t:`Unplug it, plug it back in`,next:`path_revolte_reboot`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`The machine shuts down... reboots... and shows 'FEED ME' again immediately. A gleeful 8-bit laugh comes out of the speaker with it. It is cleverer than you.`},{t:`Percussive maintenance with the hammer`,req:`hammer`,next:`path_revolte_hammer`,m:10,l:0,a:-20,b:20,r:`BAM! You bring it down on the casing with precision. The display now has a crack in it, and out of sheer fear the machine spits black coffee on the spot.`}]},{id:`cof_revolte_2a`,title:`Machine Love`,reqStory:`path_revolte_hammer`,text:`You go past the machine later. It hums quietly when it sees you. A pixel heart appears on the display with the words: 'MASTER RECOGNISED'. In the dispensing tray lies a single, perfectly wrapped biscuit that it has evidently been saving for you.`,opts:[{t:`Stroke the machine`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You pat the dented casing. 'Good girl.' She purrs (or the fan is catching). A wonderful, dysfunctional friendship.`},{t:`Eat the biscuit in triumph`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`The biscuit tastes of submission and chocolate. Colleagues stare enviously, because all they get is error codes. You have tamed the beast.`}]},{id:`cof_revolte_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Coffee Nobility`,reqStory:`path_revolte_buy`,text:`Since your donation of beans you have been treated like royalty. A delegation of colleagues heads you off: 'That was the best gear in years! We have had a whip-round so you can fetch more.' They hold out a hat full of loose change.`,opts:[{t:`Bask in the glory`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:-5,r:`You lean back against the worktop, content. 'Only the best for my team.' Even the boss nods to you as he passes. There has not been this much goodwill from above in years.`},{t:`Keep the tip for yourself`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You take the money as a 'handling fee'. The building has an official caffeine dealer, and it is you.`}]},{id:`cof_revolte_2c`,title:`Root Access`,reqStory:`path_revolte_reboot`,text:`The machine has behaved differently since the hard restart. Press 'Espresso' and you land in a hidden admin menu. 'DEBUG MODE ACTIVE'. The physics of coffee lies in your hands.`,opts:[{t:`Disable the 'laugh' sound`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`Quiet descends. You reprogram the machine to say 'Hello boss' every time you walk up instead.`},{t:`Set everything to 'Maximum'`,m:10,l:5,a:-20,b:0,r:`You put strength on 110% and temperature on 'meltdown'. What comes out is liquid dynamite. Wide awake and happy.`}]},{id:`cof_meeting_1`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Marketing Meeting`,text:`Chantal and her crew are blocking the kitchen. They are brainstorming 'feel-good management'. There are smoothies. What you need is caffeine.`,opts:[{t:`Join in`,next:`path_meeting_join`,rep:{Chantal:15},m:45,l:20,a:10,b:-5,r:`You had to talk about your feelings for 45 minutes. What you come away with is a green smoothie and some aggression.`},{t:`Wait and glare`,next:`path_meeting_wait`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:15,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`They ignore you completely. Eventually they leave. Your coffee tastes bitter and you got your way.`},{t:`Push in between them`,next:`path_meeting_push`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`You have knocked Chantal's smoothie over. 'Whoops'. Coffee acquired, enemies acquired. A green puddle spreads across the floor.`}]},{id:`cof_meeting_2a`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Bill`,reqStory:`path_meeting_push`,text:`A pink envelope is lying on your desk. Subject: 'Damages, Trainers & Emotional Distress'. Chantal is claiming €50 for cleaning the shoes you ruined with a smoothie 'the other day'.`,opts:[{t:`Shred the envelope`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`The shredder eats the pink paper. Chantal will hate you and she can prove nothing. Escalation accepted.`},{t:`Send a counter-invoice: 'working time'`,rep:{Chantal:-15},m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:5,r:`You invoice her €150 for 'IT support and psychological care'. Stalemate. Chantal stops saying hello to you from that moment on.`},{t:`Pay up and buy peace`,rep:{Chantal:10},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You put €50 in the envelope. It hurts, and the war is (possibly) over. Your wallet weeps.`}]},{id:`cof_meeting_2b`,title:`The 'Breath Ambassador'`,reqStory:`path_meeting_join`,text:`Because you showed such 'great energy' at the smoothie meeting, you have been appointed 'Breath Ambassador' for IT without anybody asking. A parcel of incense sticks is on your desk with a note: 'Spread love in the server room!'`,opts:[{t:`Bin the lot`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Away with it. You want to be an admin, not a guru. Chantal asks after your aura later, disappointed.`},{t:`Take on the role`,rep:{Chantal:15},m:10,l:20,a:-10,b:-5,r:`You light a stick. From this point you officially spend 2 hours a day on 'atmosphere maintenance'. The boss thinks it is a fire drill.`},{t:`Pass the parcel on to Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:5,Chantal:-5},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`'Here you go, Kevin, for your apprenticeship.' Kevin is delighted. He is now smoking out Stores. And your name appears nowhere.`}]},{id:`cof_meeting_2c`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Cautionary Example`,reqStory:`path_meeting_wait`,text:`You walk past the meeting room. Chantal is giving a presentation on 'toxic vibes'. On the screen is a photograph of YOU, taken without your knowledge, glaring at the coffee machine. Caption: 'The Energy Vampire'.`,opts:[{t:`Burst in and shout 'Slander!'`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:5,l:0,a:20,b:10,r:`You make a scene. Which unfortunately proves her point exactly. 'There you have it. Aggression!' calls Chantal. You have lost.`},{t:`Photograph it and use it as your profile picture`,rep:{Chantal:3},m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:5,r:`You take on the role. Your new Teams profile picture is 'The Energy Vampire'. Colleagues find it funny. Chantal is confused.`},{t:`Take out the fuse`,rep:{Chantal:-15},m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Snap. Projector off. Presentation over. You walk on, whistling. Nobody can prove it was you.`}]},{id:`cof_milk_1`,title:`High Noon in the Kitchen`,text:`Bernd from down the corridor (the one who heats fish in the microwave) reaches for the very last carton of long-life milk. Your hand lands on it at the same instant. Your eyes meet. The air crackles. Somewhere in the background, western music is playing quietly.`,opts:[{t:`Be generous and let him go first`,next:`path_milk_yield`,m:2,l:0,a:10,b:-5,r:`You let go. Karma points! And then the shock: Bernd pours the entire litre into his fruit tea. All of it. Down to the last drop. What a monster.`},{t:`Scorched earth: crush the carton`,next:`path_milk_destroy`,m:2,l:0,a:-10,b:10,r:`You squeeze. Firmly. SPLAT! The carton bursts and a white tsunami pours out across the kitchen floor. You bellow: 'IF I CANNOT HAVE IT, NOBODY CAN!'`},{t:`Demand a duel: rock, paper, scissors`,next:`path_milk_duel`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Rock beats scissors. A clean win! You claim the trophy. Bernd withdraws, beaten, muttering something about 'best of three', and the milk is already open.`}]},{id:`cof_milk_2a`,title:`The Rematch`,reqStory:`path_milk_duel`,text:`Bernd heads you off at the copier. He looks restless and is holding a coin. 'That business with the milk was luck, Miller. I demand satisfaction. Heads or tails for the last biscuit in the meeting room?'`,opts:[{t:`Take the bet`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`The coin flies. You win again. Bernd very nearly collapses.`},{t:`'Luck is part of the skill.'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You leave him standing there. Bernd mutters something about 'chicken', and you know the rule: stop while you are winning.`}]},{id:`cof_milk_2b`,title:`Calcium Deficiency`,reqStory:`path_milk_yield`,text:`You run into Bernd again. He looks extremely pleased with himself and pats his stomach. 'Thanks again for the milk. My tea was particularly creamy today. You have to treat yourself now and then, do you not?'`,opts:[{t:`'Mind your arteries.'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Bernd only laughs. 'My bones are made of steel!' Your generosity is being read as weakness here, unmistakably.`},{t:`'That one was past its date, actually...'`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Bernd's colour turns green. 'What? Why are you only telling me now?!' He runs for the toilet. Revenge is a dish best served cold.`}]},{id:`cof_milk_2c`,title:`The Embargo`,reqStory:`path_milk_destroy`,text:`There is a new sign on the kitchen door (laminated!): 'Owing to the wilful destruction of dairy products, the fridge is under video surveillance with immediate effect. Signed, Facilities Management.' Every colleague now has to register their milk at Reception.`,opts:[{t:`Nod with pride`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:10,r:`You have made a statement. Inconvenient for everybody, and nobody will dare take your milk again. Respect through fear.`},{t:`'Who would do such a thing?'`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Colleagues whisper. 'Kevin, obviously.' You nod eagerly. Scapegoats matter to the mood of a building.`}]},{id:`cof_juergen_1`,title:`The Chatterbox`,text:`Jürgen from Sales is blocking the coffee machine. He grins broadly at you: 'All right, mate? Taking a break as well? Listen, I absolutely MUST tell you about my new robot mower. It has GPS-assisted edge mode now!'`,opts:[{t:`Put the noise-cancelling headphones on`,req:`headphones`,next:`path_juergen_nc`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You put them on, nod amiably and start some Norwegian black metal. Jürgen's mouth carries on moving in silence. Heavenly quiet.`},{t:`Listen politely and die inside`,next:`path_juergen_listen`,m:20,l:10,a:15,b:0,r:`20 minutes later you know the difference between a mulching plug and side discharge. Part of your soul has left your body. Jürgen makes a threat: 'Tomorrow I will tell you about my heat pump!'`},{t:`Shout 'OH GOD, THE SERVER!' and run`,next:`path_juergen_run`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You fake a fatal system crash and sprint out of the kitchen. Freedom tastes good as well.`}]},{id:`cof_juergen_2a`,title:`A Silent Conversation`,reqStory:`path_juergen_nc`,text:`Jürgen is leaning against your desk and you did not hear him come. The headphones are still on. He is gesturing wildly and is evidently asking you something. You hear nothing whatsoever apart from double bass drums.`,opts:[{t:`Just give him a 'thumbs up'`,m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:5,r:`You grin and hold up a 👍. Jürgen beams, claps you on the shoulder and goes. 10 min later an email arrives: 'Thanks for helping with the move on Saturday!'. Damn.`},{t:`Lift an ear cup: 'EH?!'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`You raise one cup. Jürgen: '...whether you could take a look at my printer... never mind, you are busy.' Off he goes.`},{t:`Shake your head in silence`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You shake your head sadly. Jürgen looks stricken: 'Oh, I had no idea. My condolences.' He walks quietly away. What it was about, you have no idea. It worked.`}]},{id:`cof_juergen_2b`,title:`Seasonal Performance Factor`,reqStory:`path_juergen_listen`,text:`You only wanted to nip out for water. Jürgen is already lying in wait: 'Ah! There you are! I promised you the data sheets on flow temperature. Have a look here on my tablet...'`,opts:[{t:`Fake a phantom call`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`You hold your silent phone to your ear: 'Yes, sir? Right away!' and run. Jürgen calls after you: 'We will talk about the buffer tank later!'`},{t:`Correct his technical mistake`,m:30,l:-10,a:15,b:0,r:`You only wanted a brief moment of being right. Now you are stuck in a 30-minute debate about ground source versus air source.`},{t:`Play dead`,m:10,l:10,a:10,b:0,r:`You stare straight through him. Jürgen talks for 10 minutes solid, then notices you are not blinking and leaves, put out. 'I will send you the PDF...'`}]},{id:`cof_juergen_2c`,title:`Coffee Service`,reqStory:`path_juergen_run`,text:`Jürgen is at your desk, setting down a steaming mug. 'Here. You shot off earlier because of that server crash. Poor sod. Sugar, no milk, the way you like it.'`,opts:[{t:`'I have my own fuel.'`,req:`energy`,m:5,l:-20,a:0,b:0,r:`You pull the can out of your bag. *HISS*. 'That is my fuel.' You put the thing away in three swallows. Jürgen backs off, alarmed: 'All right, all right, steady on...' He is gone before your heart starts racing.`},{t:`Accept it gratefully and drink`,m:15,l:-5,a:-10,b:0,r:`The coffee brings you back to life. Unfortunately Jürgen sits down on your desk: 'Right, where was I... that is it, the robot mower!' You listen, because you are in his debt.`},{t:`'What do you want?'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Jürgen laughs: 'Just being nice! Honestly, you IT lot are always so paranoid.' He walks off shaking his head. The coffee tastes of guilt and is delicious.`}]},{id:`cof_loot_1`,title:`Repair Kit`,text:`The caretaker has left materials lying about. Unattended. A rare sight in this office.`,opts:[{t:`Take the duct tape`,loot:`tape`,next:`path_loot_tape`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`An almost full roll of gaffer. Always useful. You make it disappear, quickly.`},{t:`Take the cable ties`,loot:`zip_ties`,next:`path_loot_zip`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`A bundle of cable ties. Handy. The black sort, UV-resistant. A good catch.`}]},{id:`cof_loot_2a`,char:`Egon`,title:`The Hunt for the Gold`,reqStory:`path_loot_tape`,text:`Egon comes into the kitchen swearing. ''Ere! Have you seen my gaffer? The lid has come off the bin and I have to tape it! That was the good roll!'`,opts:[{t:`Offer a tip: 'Use chewing gum.'`,rep:{Egon:-5},m:5,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`Egon raises an eyebrow. 'Chewing gum? Am I MacGyver?' He shakes his head at the 'office lads' and goes.`},{t:`'Nope, no idea.'`,rep:{Egon:-2},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Egon kicks the bin. 'Bloody thieves in this place! You have to chain everything down!' Off he stomps, furious.`},{t:`Hand it over honestly`,rem:`tape`,rep:{Egon:5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You pull the roll out of your bag. 'I only wanted to... keep it safe.' Egon snatches it out of your hand. 'Yes, yes. Hands off.'`}]},{id:`cof_loot_2b`,char:`Egon`,title:`Nothing Holding It`,reqStory:`path_loot_zip`,text:`The dishwasher hose has come loose. Egon is kneeling in front of it. 'My cable ties have gone! I had a whole bundle! Now I have to hold this in place until the glue dries (30 minutes).'`,opts:[{t:`Feign sympathy and leave`,rep:{Egon:-2},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`'Best of luck, Egon!' You leave him to suffer. You need those ties more urgently for the cable management at your own desk.`},{t:`Donate the ties`,rem:`zip_ties`,rep:{Egon:10},m:10,l:-5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You give him the ties back. 'Oh, cheers, lad! You are saving my back.' Egon owes you one.`},{t:`'Have you not got any tape?'`,rep:{Egon:-5},m:5,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`'Tape will not hold in that heat, expert!' He is annoyed. You keep your amusement and your cable ties.`}]},{id:`cof_table_1`,title:`Wobbly Table`,text:`The standing table in the kitchen wobbles appallingly. The coffee nearly slops over the rim. It is that one millimetre that drives you mad.`,opts:[{t:`Tighten the screws brutally`,req:`screw`,next:`path_table_screw`,m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You drive the screws into the floor until the metal grinds. The table does not move by a micrometre any more. It is one with the foundations.`},{t:`Beer mat underneath`,next:`path_table_coaster`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`The classic. An old beer mat ('Gasthof zur Post') wedged under the leg. Peace.`},{t:`Kick the table leg off`,req:`hammer`,next:`path_table_kick`,m:5,l:0,a:-20,b:20,r:`You swing the hammer. CRASH! The leg buckles, the table comes down. 'There. Nothing wobbles now', you say, satisfied.`}]},{id:`cof_table_2a`,char:`Egon`,title:`Built to Last`,reqStory:`path_table_screw`,text:`The caretaker is at the table, going red and sweating. He is hauling at it with both hands. 'Who has welded this thing down?! I have to mop in here! It will not move a millimetre!'`,opts:[{t:`'That was quality work.'`,rep:{Egon:-5},m:5,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Egon stares at you. 'You have drilled through the screed into the underfloor heating!' Oops. The table is rock solid, mind.`},{t:`Take flight`,rep:{Egon:-2},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You whistle innocently and go. Behind you, you can already hear Egon setting a crowbar to it. The table wins.`}]},{id:`cof_table_2b`,char:`Kevin`,title:`Low-Rider`,reqStory:`path_table_coaster`,text:`The beer mat has gone. The table is now only 60cm high. Kevin is standing proudly beside it with a saw in his hand. 'The mat was annoying me. So I sawed the other three legs down. Nothing wobbles now!'`,opts:[{t:`Ask him: 'And when it wobbles again?'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Kevin thinks about it. 'Then I saw some more.' It dawns on you: in a week we will be eating off the floor.`},{t:`Praise him: 'Genius!'`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:-5,r:`Kevin beams. You drink your coffee squatting from now on. It looks like a nursery, and ergonomically it makes a change.`}]},{id:`cof_table_2c`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Memorial`,reqStory:`path_table_kick`,text:`The wrecked table is still lying there. Now there is red barrier tape round it. A sign from Chantal stands in front of it: 'DECONSTRUCTED WORKSPACE – An installation on the collapse of the performance society.'`,opts:[{t:`Give it a kick`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:15,r:`You kick the heap of scrap. It clatters. The bystanders applaud. 'So brave! So radical!' The world has gone mad.`},{t:`Pass yourself off as the artist`,rep:{Chantal:10},m:10,l:20,a:-10,b:10,r:`You stand beside it and nod profoundly. 'Yes, the hammer symbolised digital transformation.' Chantal takes photographs for LinkedIn. Your unofficial job title is visionary.`}]},{id:`cof_sticky_1`,title:`The Sticky Button`,text:`Disaster! The life-critical 'Double Espresso' button is stuck fast. A brown, syrupy rim gives it away: somebody has spilled something sweet here. The button does not budge a millimetre.`,opts:[{t:`Surgery with the screwdriver`,req:`screw`,next:`path_sticky_fixed`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`With the precision of a watchmaker you lever the button out, scrape the 'sugar concrete' away and put it back in. *Click*. A beautiful sound.`},{t:`Just hit it`,next:`path_sticky_broken`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`BAM! SNAP! The button breaks off and sails in a high arc under the fridge. Oops. The choice is now between 'Hot Water' and 'System Error'.`},{t:`Give up and drink tea`,next:`path_sticky_tea`,m:2,l:-5,a:0,b:0,r:`You resign yourself to it and take a peppermint teabag. It tastes of defeat and toothpaste.`}]},{id:`cof_sticky_2a`,title:`The Maintenance Backlog`,reqStory:`path_sticky_fixed`,text:`Since you were the only one who repaired the machine, you now count as the 'coffee officer'. A queue of colleagues is standing outside your office. 'Can you have a look? The milk is not frothing clockwise!'`,opts:[{t:`Put up a sign: 'IT, not a café!'`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`You send the lot of them away. They grumble, and you have your peace.`},{t:`Offer the service for a fee`,m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`You charge chocolate for every repair. Your desk is a sweet shop now.`}]},{id:`cof_sticky_2b`,title:`The Sabotage Investigation`,reqStory:`path_sticky_broken`,text:`A notice is hanging on the machine: 'Owing to vandalism (button broken off) there will be filter coffee from the pot only.' The mood in the office is aggressive. Everybody is hunting for the culprit.`,opts:[{t:`Blame Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:-5,r:`It is always Kevin. He has to make the filter coffee now. Your conscience gives a brief twinge; the espresso was worth the sacrifice.`},{t:`Join the outrage loudly: 'Unbelievable!'`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You mingle with the crowd and rail against 'these vandals'. Nobody suspects you. The cover is perfect.`}]},{id:`cof_sticky_2c`,char:`Gabi`,title:`The Tea Drinker`,reqStory:`path_sticky_tea`,text:`You are seen with your teacup. The rumour spreads: 'Miller has stopped drinking coffee. Is he ill? Burnout? Or pregnant?' Colleagues have treated you conspicuously carefully ever since.`,opts:[{t:`'The button was simply broken.'`,rep:{Gabi:-2},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'Oh, right.' The spell is broken. Gabi takes the biscuits away with her again. Reality is hard.`},{t:`Make use of the rumour`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`You cough quietly and look pained. Gabi brings you biscuits. 'For your nerves.' Life as a supposed invalid suits you well.`}]},{id:`cof_hack_1`,title:`The Service Port`,text:`You discover a USB maintenance port on the back of the coffee machine. The display shows 'INSERT SERVICE KEY'. It is tempting. Very tempting.`,opts:[{t:`Plug the boot stick in and load the script`,req:`usb_stick`,next:`path_hack_root`,m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`HACK SUCCESS! You have activated 'Developer Mode'. The coffee now runs twice as fast and costs nothing. Neo in the Matrix had a smaller moment than this.`},{t:`Try the Konami code`,next:`path_hack_glitch`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`Up, up, down, down, left, right... The display flickers wildly. It beeps three times, loudly. You hope that was a 'cheat code' and not self-destruction.`}]},{id:`cof_hack_2a`,title:`God Mode`,reqStory:`path_hack_root`,text:`Since your hack the machine has greeted you with 'HELLO ADMIN' and played an 8-bit tune. The boss is standing beside it, staring at his display, which shows nothing but 'PLEASE INSERT COIN'. He looks suspiciously across at your brim-full free cup.`,opts:[{t:`'You only have to stroke the machine.'`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:10,r:`The boss strokes the machine. Nothing happens. He knows he is being made fun of. You grin into your coffee. Worth it.`},{t:`'That is a firmware bug!'`,m:10,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`'Really? See to it, Miller!' He goes. Phew. Your privileges survive, and now you have to look as though you are working.`}]},{id:`cof_hack_2b`,title:`The Language Barrier`,reqStory:`path_hack_glitch`,text:`Your key combination has evidently changed the language settings. The menu is now entirely in Mandarin. A queue of desperate colleagues stands in front of it. Kevin has accidentally pulled 'Hot Water with Lemon' instead of 'Hot Chocolate'.`,opts:[{t:`Use the Google Translate app`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:-10,r:`You hold your phone up to it and save the day. You are the hero, having caused the problem yourself. That is true IT consulting.`},{t:`'This is a cyber attack from China!'`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:15,r:`Panic breaks out. The boss wants to pull the internet cable. Possibly an overreaction on your part; nobody suspects you.`}]},{id:`cof_chewing_1`,title:`Acoustic Torture`,text:`Sabine is standing right next to you. In her hand: a crisp, juicy Granny Smith. She bites into it. *CRUNCH*. Then she chews. With her mouth wide open. *SMACK... SMACK... SLURP*. It sounds like somebody dipping wellingtons into a bucket of mayonnaise.`,opts:[{t:`Switch the noise cancelling on at once`,req:`headphones`,next:`path_chewing_nc`,m:2,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`Click. The world falls silent. Sabine works her jaw like a ruminant and is evidently saying something to you, and all that reaches you is a gentle wash of surf. You simply nod amiably and smile.`},{t:`Almost crush the stress ball`,req:`stressball`,next:`path_chewing_ball`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You channel the whole of your hatred into the red foam ball. Your knuckles stand out white. The ball whimpers quietly under the pressure. Sabine chews on, unimpressed.`},{t:`A passive-aggressive remark`,next:`path_chewing_rude`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`You ask loudly: 'Tell me, have you swallowed a microphone or are you rehearsing for a horror film?' Sabine freezes with her mouth full. Deadly silence. The mood is on the floor.`}]},{id:`cof_chewing_2a`,title:`The Blind Nod`,reqStory:`path_chewing_nc`,text:`Later in the day Sabine comes over to you, beaming. 'Marvellous that you are doing that! I told everybody you had volunteered to defrost the fridge. You nodded so nicely in the kitchen earlier!'`,opts:[{t:`Clear the misunderstanding up`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`Sabine bursts into tears. 'And I thought you were helpful!' You are the villain of the department now, and all you wanted was to listen to music.`},{t:`Clean it through gritted teeth`,m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:-10,r:`You defrost the freezer compartment. It is cold, wet and revolting. Note to self: never nod when you cannot hear.`}]},{id:`cof_chewing_2b`,title:`Material Fatigue`,reqStory:`path_chewing_ball`,text:`You find red crumbs in your bag. Your stress ball did not survive the battle against Sabine's chewing. It has burst and spread its foam innards over your laptop.`,opts:[{t:`Try to tape it together`,req:`tape`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You wind duct tape round what is left. It now looks like a red potato that has had an accident. It barely works any more.`},{t:`Hold a small funeral at the bin`,rem:`stressball`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You throw the remains in the bin. He died a hero. Rest in peace, little ball.`},{t:`Simply blow the remains away`,m:3,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`You blow the foam crumbs off the laptop. A small red cloud sails across the open-plan office and one crumb lands in Sabine's coffee. She chews on, unimpressed.`}]},{id:`cof_chewing_2c`,title:`The Fruit War`,reqStory:`path_chewing_rude`,text:`Sabine has sworn revenge. Since your remark she has pointedly eaten nothing but soft things when you are present – while glaring at you throughout. Today there is a banana on your keyboard. A threat?`,opts:[{t:`Eat the banana pointedly`,m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You peel the banana and eat it without breaking eye contact. Sabine is confused and withdraws. Victory.`},{t:`Get frightened`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Who knows where that banana has been? You handle it with a tissue and dispose of it. The psychological war has begun.`}]},{id:`cof_gossip_1`,title:`Gossip at the Water Cooler`,text:`You hear Ms Gräte whispering: 'The boss was on a 'positive leadership' seminar yesterday. He goes completely off the deep end now if anybody says the word 'problem'. He will only hear 'challenge'. Say 'problem' and you get threatened with dismissal on the spot.'`,opts:[{t:`Join the conversation`,next:`path_gossip_caught`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:10,r:`You nod eagerly and join in the bitching. Somebody clears their throat behind you. The boss is staring at you, tapping his watch and writing your name down. The group breaks up in a panic.`},{t:`Ignore it and fetch coffee`,m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You let it in one ear and out the other. 'Not my circus, not my monkeys.' You take your cup and return to your desk without a word. Better safe than sorry.`}]},{id:`cof_gossip_2a`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Mindset Interrogation`,reqStory:`path_gossip_caught`,text:`The boss summons you to his office. He is smiling with some effort. 'Miller, I heard you in the kitchen earlier. I want to be certain that we are 'aligned'. How is the current project going? Are there... difficulties?' He waits, watching for one particular word.`,opts:[{t:`'A fantastic growth opportunity!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`The boss looks briefly confused, then nods his approval. 'Wow. That is more positive than my own coach. Keep it up!' He makes himself a note: 'Miller = visionary'.`},{t:`'Yes, we have an enormous problem.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-10},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:20,r:`The permanent smile develops cracks. 'PROBLEM?! We have no problems! We have thorns in the eye of success!' He gives you a 20-minute lecture on positivity. You come away with a headache.`},{t:`'Nothing but exciting challenges!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:-10,r:`The boss breathes out in relief. 'Excellent! That is the spirit! Here, take a cookie.' He tosses you an individually wrapped biscuit. You are safe.`}]},{id:`cof_chef_title`,title:`Title Wars in the Canteen`,text:`You hear loud shouting from the kitchen. The head of the canteen is waving a ladle about wildly: 'I am no mere COOK! I am a *Senior Nutrition Artist* and a *Food Experience Manager*! Call me 'cook' one more time and you get over-salted soup until you retire!'`,opts:[{t:`'Mr Cook? The soup is cold!'`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`The ladle stops mid-swing. He turns round slowly, and his gaze narrows and becomes very personal. The blacklist of the canteen is written down nowhere, and from today you are on it. Your next schnitzel will be of shoe-leather quality.`},{t:`'Good morning, maestro!'`,m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`He pauses, straightens his hat and smiles, flattered. 'Somebody with culture at last!' You get an extra large helping of pudding today.`},{t:`Listen with an amused grin`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`'Nutrition Artist'... is that so. If he is an artist, why does the bolognese always taste of cardboard? You keep the thought to yourself.`}]},{id:`cof_premium_hack_1`,title:`The 'Gold' Mode`,text:`You are standing in front of the machine. Your stomach rumbles. The display says: 'PREMIUM ROAST - BOARD ONLY (card required)'. For the foot soldiers there is only 'water with brown colouring' at €2.50.`,opts:[{t:`Mash buttons at random`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`ERROR 404. The machine locks itself for 5 minutes. You stare at the progress bar. Well done.`},{t:`Pay €2.50 through gritted teeth`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You put the money in. The coffee tastes of burnt tyres and defeat.`},{t:`Espresso, then cover the sensor`,next:`path_premium_audit`,m:5,l:10,a:-20,b:0,r:`The machine beeps quietly. The display shows: 'WELCOME MASTER'. Golden liquid flows into your cup. It is the best coffee of your life. Free.`},{t:`'Pay' with the hammer`,req:`hammer`,next:`path_premium_broken`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:20,r:`CLONG! You strike the coin slot. The casing dents and a 50-cent coin falls out. No coffee to be had, and you are up on the deal.`}]},{id:`cof_premium_hack_2a`,title:`The Reckoning`,reqStory:`path_premium_audit`,text:`An all-staff email from Financial Control: 'Attention! We have a discrepancy in the premium coffee stock. 1 cup is missing. Consumption will be reconciled against the security cameras with immediate effect.'`,opts:[{t:`'The machine was leaking!'`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:10,r:`You hit 'Reply All'. 'Saw coffee water running out. Somebody tell facilities!' Everybody thanks you for your vigilance. Genius.`},{t:`Sweat nervously`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You simply hope the camera resolution was too poor. The coffee was worth it; you do not dare set foot in the kitchen again today.`}]},{id:`cof_premium_hack_2b`,char:`Egon`,title:`Vandalism Alert`,reqStory:`path_premium_broken`,text:`The caretaker is standing in front of the dented machine. He is holding up an e-fit that looks suspiciously like you (with a moustache). 'Whoever that was... I will find him. Nobody dents my lady.'`,opts:[{t:`Push the blame onto the hauliers`,rep:{Egon:2},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`'It was already like that when it was delivered, Egon!' Egon scratches his head. 'True... the boxes did look rough.' Suspicion averted.`},{t:`Slip away quietly`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You reverse out of the room. The business with the 50 cents is something you tell nobody.`}]},{id:`cof_iot_fail_1`,title:`The Dangerous IoT Upgrade`,text:`You cannot believe your eyes: somebody has bodged a cheap 'smart plug' (brand: 'China Export') in between the socket and the coffee machine. The casing is melting already, it is arcing blue and there is an acrid smell of burnt plasticiser. Fire risk: red.`,opts:[{t:`Pull the plug at once`,next:`path_iot_sabotage`,m:10,l:-5,a:30,b:30,r:`SNAP! A shower of sparks. You have saved the building. In storms the head of marketing, scarlet in the face: 'MY PROTOTYPE! I worked on the blockchain-based 'Coffee Cloud' for weeks! You Luddite!'`},{t:`Wait and drink Coke`,next:`path_iot_fire`,m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`Not your hardware, not your fire. You crack open a Coke with a hiss and watch. WHUMP! A jet of flame. Then the sprinklers go off and turn the corridor into a wetland habitat.`}]},{id:`cof_iot_fail_2a`,title:`The Crypto War`,reqStory:`path_iot_sabotage`,text:`The head of marketing has lodged an official complaint. He is claiming damages for the 'lost profit' of his planned 'Coffee-Coin' ICO, which you prevented by pulling the plug.`,opts:[{t:`Bring Egon in`,rep:{Egon:5},m:10,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`You tell the caretaker. Egon storms into the marketing office with a pair of bolt croppers. 'No unauthorised equipment!' The shouting carries as far as the third floor.`},{t:`Read him the VDE regulation`,m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:5,r:`You quote sections on fire safety at him. He falls asleep after 2 minutes. The complaint is dropped on grounds of 'boredom'.`}]},{id:`cof_iot_fail_2b`,title:`The Wetland Habitat`,reqStory:`path_iot_fire`,text:`The fire brigade has gone and the kitchen is under water. The head of marketing stands weeping in front of his charred smart plug. 'Why did nobody say anything?!'`,opts:[{t:`'Is this that liquid cooling?'`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`A cruel joke. It had to be made. The head of marketing hates you from this moment on, and the IT department celebrates you as a legend.`},{t:`Shrug it off: 'I was in a meeting'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`The perfect excuse. That you stood beside it with a Coke appears in no minutes anywhere. You stay dry.`}]},{id:`cof_descaling_1`,title:`Limescale Coronary`,text:`The coffee machine is blinking an aggressive red: 'SYSTEM SCALED UP - PLEASE CLEAN'. The coffee drips into the cup once a second now, like a leaking gutter. The pump groans audibly.`,opts:[{t:`Stick an 'OUT OF ORDER' sign on it and vanish`,next:`path_descale_fake`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You stick a note over the display and make yourself scarce. Colleagues sigh in disappointment and shuffle back to work. The problem is not solved; it is delegated, and that counts.`},{t:`Heroically start the cleaning cycle`,next:`path_descale_hero`,m:10,l:-10,a:40,b:0,r:`You press the button. A fatal error. The display shows: 'Cleaning in progress... Time remaining: 45 minutes'. An angry queue forms behind you at once. 'Nice one, Miller! Now nobody gets anything!' You are booed.`},{t:`Ignore it and let it drip`,next:`path_descale_ignore`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You stare stoically at the spout. Drip... Drip... After 5 minutes you have half a cup of lukewarm, chalky brew. It tastes of misery and it contains caffeine.`}]},{id:`cof_descaling_2a`,title:`The Acid Attack`,reqStory:`path_descale_hero`,text:`The descaling is done and something is not right. The first colleague to pull a coffee spits it clean across the room. 'AGH! That tastes of battery acid! Who did not rinse it through?!'`,opts:[{t:`Whistle innocently`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You look away. 'A software fault, no doubt.' The colleague rinses his mouth out at the water cooler. That was close.`},{t:`'That is the new citrus roast.'`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`The colleague tries again, cautiously. 'Really? Hm... refreshing on the finish.' You have just started a revolting trend.`}]},{id:`cof_descaling_2b`,char:`Egon`,title:`Egon Investigates`,reqStory:`path_descale_fake`,text:`Egon the caretaker is waving your 'OUT OF ORDER' note about in the corridor. 'Which joker was that? The machine only wanted descaling! I am not your nanny!' He is looking for the culprit.`,opts:[{t:`Blame Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-5,Egon:5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:-5,r:`'The apprentice was the last one in the kitchen.' Egon nods grimly and stomps off towards the apprentice's desk. Your conscience is black and clear.`},{t:`Own up: 'I did not mean to break anything'`,rep:{Egon:2},m:5,l:-5,a:0,b:0,r:`Egon snorts. 'Typical pen-pusher. Two left hands.' He calms down, though. You are permitted to live.`}]},{id:`cof_descaling_2c`,title:`Inner Values`,reqStory:`path_descale_ignore`,text:`Your stomach is rumbling strangely. It is as though you have swallowed half a brick. There was evidently more limescale than water in that 'coffee'.`,opts:[{t:`'That is good for the bones.'`,m:2,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`Minerals matter. You persuade yourself that you are eating healthily. Pain is only weakness leaving the body.`},{t:`Drink water by the litre`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`You try to flush the sediment out of your body. You spend the rest of the afternoon in the toilet. Productivity: 0.`}]},{id:`cof_spill_1`,title:`The Brown Peril`,text:`A lake of sticky, cold coffee is spreading in front of the machine. The culprit is long gone. It is a slippery death trap, waiting to claim its next victim.`,opts:[{t:`Take one big step over it`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`With an Olympic-standard leap you clear the puddle. Not your mess, not your problem. Let the night shift go skating.`},{t:`Heroically take up the cloth and mop`,next:`path_spill_clean`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:10,l:-5,a:20,b:20,r:`You kneel on the floor and mop. At that exact moment the boss comes round the corner. 'Good God, Miller! Can you not even hold a cup? This is embarrassing!' He steps over your hand and walks off shaking his head. You are boiling with rage.`},{t:`Make a warning sign and put it up`,next:`path_spill_warn`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`You scrawl 'CAUTION: LETHAL' on a piece of paper, stand it up and leave. Shortly afterwards you hear a loud skid behind you, followed by swearing. Reading is a skill with obvious advantages.`}]},{id:`cof_spill_2a`,title:`The Sippy Cup`,reqStory:`path_spill_clean`,text:`There is a parcel from the boss on your desk. Contents: a colourful child's beaker with a lid and a spout. Note: 'So the carpets stay clean. Safety First!'.`,opts:[{t:`Throw it in the bin`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`The thing goes into the wastepaper basket with some force. You are not a toddler.`},{t:`Use the cup out of spite`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`You drink from the sippy cup, pointedly. Colleagues giggle behind their hands. It is excruciating, and the coffee does stay hot. Your rage grows with every sip.`}]},{id:`cof_spill_2b`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Workplace Accident`,reqStory:`path_spill_warn`,text:`Chantal limps past you with a bandaged ankle. She waves your note about angrily. 'That sign was far too small! I am going to report this as a workplace accident for inadequate safety signage!'`,opts:[{t:`Fight it legally: 'meets the DIN standard'`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:5,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`You have to explain to her for 10 minutes that the font size was legible. She sweeps off, offended.`},{t:`Sympathise and sacrifice the chocolate`,rep:{Chantal:10},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You give her a bar out of your drawer. She calms down at once. 'Very well. But next time you put neon on it, all right?' Problem solved.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_fight_1`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`A Row About the Fridge`,text:`Ms Elster throws your food away! 'That reeks of peanuts!' she screeches. You take her to task.`,opts:[{t:`Back down`,next:`path_elster_police`,rep:{"Frau Elster":2},m:5,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`You apologise meekly. She straightens her glasses, snorts: 'One has to think of the community!' and sweeps off. The row is over, and so is your lunch.`},{t:`'THAT WAS MY LUNCH!'`,next:`path_elster_allergy`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-5},m:10,l:0,a:20,b:10,r:`She shouts back: 'I am highly sensitive! If I so much as smell **peanuts** my throat closes up! Kindly show some consideration!' She is breathing heavily. Well, well: a sore spot found.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_fight_2a`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`The Biological Weapon`,reqStory:`path_elster_allergy`,text:`You are sitting in the kitchen opening a 'Snickers'. Ms Elster comes in, sniffs, goes chalk white and backs away. 'Is that... peanut? Are you trying to kill me?! Take it away!'`,opts:[{t:`Show consideration and put it away`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`You put the bar away. 'It is fine.' She nods gratefully and suspiciously at once. You go hungry. Nobody has died.`},{t:`Chew with relish and breathe on her`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-10},m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`You chew extra loudly. 'Mmm, crunchy.' Ms Elster flees the room in a panic. The kitchen belongs to you alone.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_fight_2b`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`The Food Police`,reqStory:`path_elster_police`,text:`Since you backed down last time, Ms Elster is cracking down. Your yoghurt has gone. In its place a note is stuck to the shelf: 'Disposed of pre-emptively, no use-by date. Signed, Elster'.`,opts:[{t:`Write a furious note back`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You write: 'Hands off my property!' and stick it to her tub.`},{t:`Relabel every shelf`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:2,l:5,a:15,b:0,r:`You label every single item of food with a date and a name so that she leaves off. It takes 10 minutes and is unspeakably tedious.`}]},{id:`cof_salary_rumor_1`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Salary Shock`,text:`You are standing behind the pillar and hear Chantal from marketing giggling: 'Yes, honestly! €500 more! Just like that, because I smiled nicely! And I can barely use Excel.' Your salary has not been adjusted for 3 years. You are very close to losing it.`,opts:[{t:`Use the anger and write your achievements down`,loot:`arg_list_1`,next:`path_salary_talk`,m:10,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You grab a napkin and scrawl your achievements down in a fury: '1000 tickets resolved, fires prevented, servers saved'. You pocket the note like a weapon. Valuable ammunition for later.`},{t:`Make a scene at Chantal`,next:`path_salary_rage`,rep:{Chantal:-15},m:5,l:0,a:20,b:10,r:`You bellow across the room: 'EXCEL IS NOT AN ART FORM!'. Chantal starts to cry. Everybody stares at you. Steam released; mental stability visibly not. Not a good look.`},{t:`Wash the anger down`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You swallow the anger down, or knead your stress ball. It changes nothing about your bank balance; your blood pressure drops marginally. You go back to work, frustrated.`}]},{id:`cof_salary_rumor_2a`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Pitch`,reqStory:`path_salary_talk`,text:`The boss sees you in the corridor. 'Ah, Miller! Good, just the man.' Your list of arguments is in your pocket. This is the moment.`,opts:[{t:`Bottle it and only say hello`,m:2,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`Courage gone. 'Morning.' He walks on. You have wasted the chance and hate yourself a little for it.`},{t:`Produce the list and ask`,req:`arg_list_1`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:10,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`You reel your achievements off. The boss is impressed (and slightly intimidated). 'All right, all right! We will talk about a bonus.' A partial win!`}]},{id:`cof_salary_rumor_2b`,title:`The HR Meeting`,reqStory:`path_salary_rage`,text:`An email from HR: 'Subject: Incident in the kitchenette'. They would like to talk about your 'social competence' and 'anger management'.`,opts:[{t:`Attend and apologise`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You have to nod for 30 minutes and promise to do better. It is humiliating. Chantal grins at you in the corridor afterwards. Your hatred grows.`},{t:`'Forget' the appointment`,rep:{Chantal:-10},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:20,r:`You simply do not go. Rebellious and stupid. There is an official written warning in your file now. Your pride is intact.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_flex_1`,char:`Markus`,title:`The Show-Off`,text:`Markus from Sales has planted himself in front of the machine. He rolls his sleeve up and holds his wrist under your nose. 'All right, admin? Take a proper look. This watch costs more than your entire car.' He grins his broad winner's grin.`,opts:[{t:`A well-aimed throw with the stress ball`,req:`stressball`,next:`path_markus_hit`,rep:{Markus:-15,"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:0,a:-20,b:30,r:`SMACK! A direct hit on the nose. Markus yelps like a kicked poodle. Unfortunately the boss was standing in the doorway. There will be trouble.`},{t:`Counter drily: 'Is it leased?'`,next:`path_markus_roast`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:5,r:`His grin sets. He goes red and stammers something about an 'investment'. The colleagues standing round burst out laughing. A win on every front.`},{t:`Put the headphones on and ignore him`,req:`headphones`,rep:{Markus:-2},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Click. Noise cancelling on. Gentle Mozart reaches you while Markus moves his mouth in silence. You draw your coffee at leisure. Peace.`},{t:`Wait submissively`,next:`path_markus_servant`,rep:{Markus:5},m:20,l:0,a:20,b:0,r:`You wait obediently for 20 minutes until he has finished his monologue on 'assets' and 'mindset'. Your coffee arrives tasting bitterly of humiliation.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_flex_2a`,char:`Markus`,title:`Compensation`,reqStory:`path_markus_hit`,text:`Markus is now wearing an enormous plaster on his nose (wildly excessive). He waves a form about in your face. 'That was assault! Either you sign this official apology or I ring my solicitor!'`,opts:[{t:`Back down and sign`,rep:{Markus:5},m:5,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`You sign. Markus grins in triumph and hangs the note on his office door. Everybody can read that you are sorry. Your blood boils.`},{t:`Threaten him again`,req:`stressball`,rep:{Markus:-10},m:5,l:-5,a:-5,b:10,r:`You get the stress ball out again. Markus flinches and runs off. The problem is postponed rather than solved.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_flex_2b`,char:`Markus`,title:`The Proof`,reqStory:`path_markus_roast`,text:`Your line hit Markus' ego hard. He comes over to you with his laptop. 'Leased? Do not make me laugh! Look at my crypto portfolio! I am rich! RICH!' He pushes the screen at you.`,opts:[{t:`Read it out loud: 'Minus 60 per cent?!'`,rep:{Markus:-15},m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:5,r:`You point at the red line. Markus snaps the laptop shut in a panic. 'That is only... a correction! Buy the dip!' He runs off in tears.`},{t:`Wave him away, uninterested`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`'Yes, yes, Markus.' You leave him standing there. Nothing hurts a show-off more than indifference.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_flex_2c`,char:`Markus`,title:`The Coaching`,reqStory:`path_markus_servant`,text:`Because you listened to him, Markus now regards you as his 'student'. He sends you WhatsApp voice notes at 06:00: 'Good morning, champ! Time to hustle! Fetch me a coffee, it teaches humility!'`,opts:[{t:`Fetch the coffee without a word`,rep:{Markus:10},m:10,l:0,a:25,b:0,r:`You bring him the coffee. He pats you on the head. 'Good boy.' You die a thousand deaths inside.`},{t:`Block him and ignore him`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You block his number. Markus turns up at your desk later, baffled: 'My phone is playing up.' You merely shrug.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_sad_1`,char:`Gabi`,title:`A Bereavement in the Post Room`,text:`Gabi from the post room is sitting on the corner bench in the break room, sobbing. In her hand she is holding a brown, shrivelled lump. 'My little Spike is dead! Just gone from us!'`,opts:[{t:`Listen patiently`,next:`path_gabi_listen`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:45,l:-15,a:20,b:10,r:`You sit through a 45-minute eulogy for a succulent. Your coffee goes cold. Gabi comes away 'so understood'; you come away dead inside and far too late.`},{t:`Donate the 'loot doughnut' as consolation`,rem:`donut`,next:`path_gabi_donut`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:-5,r:`You sacrifice your treasure. Gabi's eyes light up. Sugar heals all wounds. She munches away happily. 'You are so kind! I will get back to work.' A good deed!`},{t:`Give her an energy drink`,rem:`energy`,next:`path_gabi_energy`,rep:{Gabi:-5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`A thoroughly bad idea. The taurine hits immediately. Gabi's eyes go wide, she jumps up and runs back to the post room like a gassed hamster. There will be consequences.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_sad_2a`,char:`Gabi`,title:`Special Delivery`,reqStory:`path_gabi_donut`,text:`Gabi waves you urgently behind the palm in the corridor. 'Pssst! My saviour! This came for you. I intercepted it before the boss saw it, it looked private.' She presses a parcel into your hand.`,opts:[{t:`Thank her and take it`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`It is your Amazon order (a new gaming mouse). Gabi winks at you conspiratorially. 'Your post is safe with me!' A valuable ally.`},{t:`Promise her more sweet things`,rep:{Gabi:10},m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`You promise her the next cake from the meeting. Gabi beams. VIP status in the post round is yours.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_sad_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Site Inspection`,reqStory:`path_gabi_energy`,text:`The boss storms into the kitchen, grabs you by the arm and hauls you into the corridor. 'You wound Gabi up?! Look at this!' Through the open door of the post room you can see Gabi stacking parcels to the ceiling at piece-work speed.`,opts:[{t:`'Efficient!'`,rep:{Gabi:-5,"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`The boss comes out in red blotches on his neck. 'This is not Tetris, these are important files!' You have to help dismantle the tower before it comes down. Tedious punishment duty.`},{t:`'Not my area of responsibility.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:2,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You tear yourself free and run back to the coffee. The boss bellows after you. There will be trouble, and no climbing.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_sad_2c`,char:`Gabi`,title:`The Limpet`,reqStory:`path_gabi_listen`,text:`Halfway to the coffee machine, Gabi springs out from behind the fridge. She has been waiting for you. 'Listen, the empty pot looks so lonely... do you think a begonia would be better than a cactus?'`,opts:[{t:`'Get plastic flowers.'`,rep:{Gabi:2},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'Oh, good idea! Those do not die!' Off she runs to buy some. The corridor is yours again - only the guilty conscience follows you down it.`},{t:`Hide behind the coffee machine`,m:5,l:-5,a:15,b:0,r:`You duck out of sight. Gabi looks for you briefly, sighs loudly ('Nobody understands me except you!') and goes. That was close, and thoroughly degrading.`}]},{id:`cof_machine_broke_1`,title:`Critical Seal Failure`,text:`A trickle of hot water is shooting out of the side of the coffee machine. The brown brew is making its unstoppable way towards the hopelessly overloaded extension lead on the floor. A quiet, menacing electrical crackle is already in the air.`,opts:[{t:`Seal it with gaffer tape`,req:`tape`,next:`path_machine_tape`,m:10,l:-5,a:0,b:-10,r:`You wind half a roll of tape round the water tank. It looks like a badly done mummy, and it holds! The kitchen stays dry, the coffee flows.`},{t:`Pull the plug at once`,next:`path_machine_plug`,m:5,l:5,a:10,b:10,r:`Snap. Power off. The danger is averted. The display goes black. A collective, pained groan goes through the office.`},{t:`Walk on whistling and ignore it`,next:`path_machine_blackout`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:10,a:0,b:50,r:`You ignore the puddle. Ten minutes later: *ZZZAP*. Darkness across the whole floor. The boss storms into the corridor and bellows: 'WHO HAS BLOWN THE FUSE?! MY WORD DOCUMENT!!'`}]},{id:`cof_machine_broke_2a`,char:`Egon`,title:`Feat of Engineering`,reqStory:`path_machine_tape`,text:`Egon the caretaker stands before your tape masterpiece. He nods slowly, with approval. 'Clean work, Miller. I could not have done it better. That will hold until 2030.' He gives you a firm clap on the shoulder.`,opts:[{t:`'Duct tape sorts everything.'`,rep:{Egon:10},m:5,l:5,a:-15,b:0,r:`You swap tradesman's wisdom for a minute. It is enormously relaxing.`},{t:`Nod modestly`,rep:{Egon:10},m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:-5,r:`You enjoy the rare respect. Egon even invites you to come and look at his new cordless driver later. A good day.`}]},{id:`cof_machine_broke_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Lifesaver`,reqStory:`path_machine_plug`,text:`The boss comes in furious, then sees the scorched socket, still faintly smoking. He goes pale. 'My God... if you had not pulled it out... the whole archive! Miller, you have saved our backsides!'`,opts:[{t:`Play the hero`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":15},m:10,l:5,a:-20,b:-30,r:`'Just doing my job, sir.' He shakes your hand gratefully. 'Clock off early today. That is an order!' Music to your ears.`},{t:`'Safety comes first.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:-20,r:`Colleagues applaud quietly. The annoyance about the missing coffee has evaporated. You are the responsible rock in the surf.`}]},{id:`cof_machine_broke_2c`,title:`Enforced Break`,reqStory:`path_machine_blackout`,text:`The power is gone, the PCs are off. Instead of panic, a strange calm spreads. Somebody has passed biscuits round. Even the boss relaxes once IT has confirmed that the autosave worked.`,opts:[{t:`Tell jokes`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:10,l:10,a:-15,b:-5,r:`The mood is easy. The boss even laughs at your (harmless) joke. This unplanned team-building exercise was exactly what everybody needed.`},{t:`Enjoy the silence`,m:20,l:0,a:-25,b:-10,r:`No phone calls, no fan noise. Everybody sits in the half-dark, talking pleasantly. It is like a campfire without a fire. You properly recharge.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_learn_1`,char:`Kevin`,title:`Kevin's Worldview`,text:`Kevin is staring at the blinking server rack, fascinated. He turns to you, wide-eyed: 'Tell me... is there actually a little man in there typing all the emails and passing them on?' You wait for the punchline. None arrives. He means it in deadly earnest.`,opts:[{t:`Hand him the manual without a word`,req:`manual`,next:`path_kevin_manual`,rep:{Kevin:-2},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You press the heavy tome against his chest. 'Read chapters 1 to 10. Do not speak to me before then.' He retreats reverently into a corner. Peace at last.`},{t:`'Yes, that is the email goblin.'`,next:`path_kevin_kobold`,rep:{Kevin:5,"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:10,r:`You nod conspiratorially: 'Yes, his name is Gunter. Whatever you do, do not feed him!' Kevin is now crawling behind the rack with a torch, looking for Gunter. The boss sees it and starts to doubt the apprentice's suitability.`},{t:`Explain the technology patiently`,next:`path_kevin_explain`,rep:{Kevin:5,"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:30,l:-10,a:10,b:0,r:`You take half an hour and draw data packets on the whiteboard. Kevin nods slowly: 'Oh, right! So like a pneumatic tube, only invisible?' A small step forward.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_learn_2a`,char:`Kevin`,title:`Pneumatic Tube 2.0`,reqStory:`path_kevin_explain`,text:`Kevin has tried to put your explanation into practice. He has taped toilet roll tubes to the server fans. 'So the data slides through faster!' he calls proudly. Surprisingly, the result is a pleasantly cool draught blowing straight onto your desk.`,opts:[{t:`Enjoy it and praise him`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:2,l:5,a:-15,b:5,r:`You lean back. 'Good work, Kevin.' The draught is glorious in this heat. An innovation that actually does something, for once. You are relaxed.`},{t:`Tear the construction down`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You pull the cardboard tubes off. 'Fire safety!' Kevin looks sad. Now you are sweating again and scraping glue residue off fans. Badly played, on reflection.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_learn_2b`,char:`Kevin`,title:`The Scholar`,reqStory:`path_kevin_manual`,text:`Kevin is standing to attention in front of you. He has learned the manual by heart. 'According to page 103, paragraph 4, the administrator is entitled to a twenty-minute recovery break under elevated server load. Shall I be the doorman?'`,opts:[{t:`Send him away`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:2,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`'Give it a rest.' You carry on working. Kevin is disappointed. You have just turned down an officially sanctioned break.`},{t:`Take him up on it`,rep:{Kevin:10},m:20,l:5,a:-20,b:0,r:`You put your feet up. Kevin guards the door and turns even the boss away, citing 'page 103'. The finest apprentice of all time.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_learn_2c`,title:`Gunter's Offering`,reqStory:`path_kevin_kobold`,text:`Behind the rack you find a plate. On it, no sour milk, but a box of the finest Belgian chocolates. A note lies with it: 'For Gunter, please fix the internet.'`,opts:[{t:`Pass yourself off as Gunter and eat them`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:5,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`You munch your way through the chocolates with relish. They taste fantastic. When Kevin comes in you burp quietly. Kevin whispers reverently: 'Gunter has accepted it!'`},{t:`Frighten Kevin as Gunter`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:5,l:15,a:-15,b:5,r:`You hide and make ghostly noises: *'MORE CHOCOLATE!'* Kevin runs off screaming. You laugh until you cry.`}]},{id:`cof_birthday_cake_1`,title:`Cake in the Corridor`,text:`An enormous chocolate cake stands ownerless on the side table. A handwritten sign says: 'Help yourselves!'. It smells temptingly of cocoa and cream.`,opts:[{t:`Be suspicious`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Free food? Suspicious. Who knows how long it has been standing there. You do not touch it. Hungry, and safe.`},{t:`Take a slice`,next:`path_cake_eat`,m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`Delicious! Pure sugar shock. You shovel the slice in. Life is good.`},{t:`Take the whole cake away`,next:`path_cake_steal`,m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:20,r:`You look around – the coast is clear. You take the whole plate and carry it quickly to your office. 'For later'. Your heart pounds with greed.`}]},{id:`cof_birthday_cake_2a`,title:`The Rum Bomb`,reqStory:`path_cake_eat`,text:`Whoops. That was not only chocolate. That was 'Black Forest gateau' with 80% Stroh rum. A warmth spreads through your chest and you go slightly dizzy. The stress falls away from you and your tongue has gone furry.`,opts:[{t:`Try to look respectable`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You sit bolt upright and stare at your monitor. Whatever happens, do not be noticed. The paranoia takes the edge off the good mood.`},{t:`Enjoy the buzz`,next:`path_cake_drunk`,m:5,l:0,a:-20,b:5,r:`You lean against the wall and grin stupidly. A colleague asks you something and you only giggle. The best working day in years.`}]},{id:`cof_birthday_cake_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Meeting Crasher`,reqStory:`path_cake_steal`,text:`You are sitting in your office in front of the stolen cake when the door flies open. The boss and three Japanese investors are standing there. The boss stares at the cake, then at you. 'Miller?! That was the catering for the delegation!'`,opts:[{t:`Offer to share`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`You hold a fork out to the investor. He accepts with thanks. The situation is saved; the boss will kill you later.`},{t:`'Quality control!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:10,a:20,b:30,r:`You stammer something about a 'poison test' with your mouth full. Nobody believes you. It is unspeakably embarrassing. The Japanese bow politely to your greed.`}]},{id:`cof_elevator_stuck_1`,char:`Markus`,title:`Stuck in the Lift`,text:`Jolt. Clack. Silence. Not again! The lift stops between the second and third floor. Beside you stands Markus from Sales in a cloud of 'Eau de Success'. He grins: 'Well then, time for a spot of networking, eh?'`,opts:[{t:`Lever the lift door open`,req:`screw`,next:`path_elevator_hero`,rep:{Markus:15},m:10,l:-5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You ram the screwdriver into the gap. The door slides open with a jerk. Freedom! The other occupants are impressed: 'Alpha move, respect!'`},{t:`Press the emergency call and pray`,next:`path_elevator_tech`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:30,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`Egon answers, crackling: ''Ere! I am finishing my sandwich first. Keep your hair on.' You are trapped for 30 minutes. Your mood hits rock bottom.`},{t:`Listen to Markus bravely`,next:`path_elevator_markus`,rep:{Markus:5},m:30,l:-10,a:25,b:0,r:`He talks about his Porsche, his crypto wins and his 'mindset'. You nod apathetically and die a thousand deaths inside. He appears to be reading the nodding as agreement.`}]},{id:`cof_elevator_2a`,char:`Markus`,title:`Trapped with the Beast`,reqStory:`path_elevator_markus`,text:`Markus jumps into the lift with you at the last second. 'All right, big man! Good, just the person!' Grinning, he presses the **emergency stop button**. The lift stops hard. 'I urgently need to tell you about my new business idea. It only takes 20 minutes.'`,opts:[{t:`Scream in a panic: 'HELP!'`,rep:{Markus:3},m:5,l:0,a:30,b:0,r:`Markus laughs. 'You are so funny! But seriously: multi-level marketing for hamster food!' There is no escape. This is false imprisonment.`},{t:`Steal his show`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:20,l:0,a:-10,b:5,r:`You start telling HIM a story about your boring weekend. After 5 minutes Markus presses the button in irritation so the lift moves on. Boredom wins the day.`}]},{id:`cof_elevator_2b`,title:`Experts at Work`,reqStory:`path_elevator_tech`,text:`The lift jolts and stops. Beside you: a man in a boiler suit. His colour drains away. 'Er. I am the engineer. I was coming to repair the lift.' He presses buttons frantically. 'Damn. My toolbox is outside. We are stuck.'`,opts:[{t:`Give him the 'emergency doughnut'`,req:`donut`,m:20,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`The engineer is shaking from low blood sugar. You give him the doughnut. He calms down, kicks the door and – SNAP – it opens. 'Cheers, mate!' Sugar beats engineering more often than engineering likes to admit.`},{t:`Wait for rescue together`,m:45,l:0,a:20,b:0,r:`You both sit on the floor. The engineer weeps quietly. After 45 minutes you hear Egon laughing as he opens the door from outside. 'Well now, a coffee morning?'`}]},{id:`cof_elevator_2c`,title:`The Lift Whisperer`,reqStory:`path_elevator_hero`,text:`The lift judders and stops. The five other colleagues turn to you in unison. One holds out his car key expectantly. 'Go on then. You fixed it the other day. We are in a hurry.'`,opts:[{t:`'I am not an engineer.'`,m:30,l:0,a:15,b:-5,r:`The mood turns. 'Great. Now we have to wait.' Everybody stares at you reproachfully for 30 minutes. You are the one they blame, for not wanting to help.`},{t:`Put on a repair performance`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`You rattle the door importantly and mutter 'flux capacitor'. By coincidence it moves on. 'A genius!' whisper the colleagues.`}]},{id:`cof_miracle_1`,title:`The Small Miracle`,text:`The machine makes strange noises, rattles... and then produces the perfect coffee. Perfect temperature, hazelnut-brown crema, the smell of Italy. A statistical outlier. A unicorn in cup form.`,opts:[{t:`Take a photo for Insta`,next:`path_miracle_insta`,m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`This must be documented! You arrange your glasses and a pen decoratively beside it. '#OfficeLife #Grindset #Blessed'. One photograph is not going to be enough...`},{t:`Take it to the boss`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},next:`path_miracle_boss`,m:5,l:-5,a:5,b:-15,r:`You think strategically. You carry the holy grail carefully into the boss's office. 'Here you are, sir, this one is particularly good today.' He looks surprised.`},{t:`Enjoy it reverently on the spot`,m:10,l:5,a:-25,b:0,r:`You drink it in small sips. Every sip heals your soul a little. You ignore the phone and the world. For 5 minutes everything is fine.`}]},{id:`cof_miracle_2a`,title:`The Influencer Debacle`,reqStory:`path_miracle_insta`,text:`You try to find the perfect angle. You climb onto your office chair, pull a duckface and hold the cup up to the camera. The door opens. The entire board is standing there staring at you. You are standing on the chair. With pursed lips.`,opts:[{t:`Post the photo and await dismissal`,m:2,l:10,a:-10,b:5,r:`You take the shot. The photo is blurred and your expression is deranged. Still: 3 likes from bots! The social descent was worth it.`},{t:`Pretend it is a yoga exercise`,m:5,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`You stretch slowly. 'Office gymnastics! Important for the back!' Nobody buys it. The board move on, shaking their heads. You would like the floor to swallow you.`}]},{id:`cof_miracle_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Pearls Before Swine`,reqStory:`path_miracle_boss`,text:`The boss is delighted. 'Miller! You read minds!' He takes the cup with the perfect coffee in it... and tips in three sachets of sweetener and a splash of lactose-free long-life milk. The crema collapses instantly into grey dishwater.`,opts:[{t:`'That was a grand cru!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:5,a:5,b:5,r:`The boss only looks tired. 'It is coffee, Miller. Not a science. Go and do some work.' Your sacrifice was for nothing.`},{t:`Weep inwardly and smile`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:-10,r:`'Delicious', smacks the boss. You sacrificed the holiest thing you had and he desecrated it. He likes you slightly more for it. Your heart bleeds.`}]},{id:`cof_silence_1`,title:`Heavenly Silence`,text:`You step into the kitchen. It is empty. No fridge hum, no chewing colleague, no dripping. Nothing but absolute, golden silence. It is almost... eerily peaceful.`,opts:[{t:`Quick coffee and out`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You do not trust the peace. You fill your cup and vanish straight back into the safe noise of your office.`},{t:`Close your eyes and enjoy it`,next:`path_silence_jumpscare`,m:5,l:5,a:-20,b:0,r:`You breathe in deeply. Five minutes of Zen mode. Your blood pressure drops, and you can tell. You are one with the universe. A rare moment of peace.`},{t:`Look around uneasily: 'Where is everybody?'`,next:`path_silence_drill`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You look around. Nobody there. Nobody in the corridor either. A cold shiver runs down your spine. Something here is not right.`}]},{id:`cof_silence_2a`,title:`Cardiac Risk`,reqStory:`path_silence_jumpscare`,text:`You are deeply relaxed when somebody bellows directly into your ear: 'MAHLZEIT!!!'. It is Funny Holger from Accounts, who has crept up on you.`,opts:[{t:`Throw the stress ball on reflex`,req:`stressball`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:10,r:`Your arm twitches on reflex. The stress ball hits Holger on the head. 'Ow! Are you mad?!' He is the victim now. Serves him right.`},{t:`Spill the coffee in fright`,m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`The hot coffee lands on your shirt. Holger is helpless with laughter: 'Hahaha, you jumped!'. You are wet, scalded and thinking about murder.`}]},{id:`cof_silence_2b`,title:`Left Behind`,reqStory:`path_silence_drill`,text:`You look out of the window. Down in the car park all your colleagues are standing about waving. A fire engine pulls up. You missed the fire alarm on account of your noise-cancelling headphones (or pure ignorance).`,opts:[{t:`Hide and hope`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:20,r:`You duck under the desk. If nobody sees you, you were never there. You enjoy having the place to yourself while everybody outside freezes.`},{t:`Run down in a panic`,m:10,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You sprint down 5 storeys. You arrive at the bottom sweating and out of breath. The safety officer writes your name down: 'Too late. In a real emergency you would be crispy by now.'`}]},{id:`cof_cookie_luck_1`,title:`The Orphaned Biscuit`,text:`Next to the sugar bowl lies a single wrapped premium biscuit (caramel centre). No note, no owner in sight. The universe means well by you.`,opts:[{t:`Pocket it for later`,next:`path_cookie_save`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You let it slide into your pocket. Knowing you have an emergency ration is enormously calming. Anticipation is the finest kind of pleasure.`},{t:`Eat it at once`,next:`path_cookie_mystery`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`Rustle. Munch. The sugar floods your brain. Happy hormones put up a brief fight against the stress. And it is gone.`}]},{id:`cof_cookie_2a`,title:`The Biscuit Fairy`,reqStory:`path_cookie_mystery`,text:`You come back to your desk... and there is *another* one! Right in the middle of your keyboard. Caramel centre again. Who is doing this? And why?`,opts:[{t:`Play detective`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You examine the wrapper for fingerprints. Nothing. The uncertainty is driving you mad. Was it the boss? Or only the cleaner after all?`},{t:`Do not ask, just eat`,m:5,l:5,a:-20,b:0,r:`Never look a gift horse in the mouth. You eat the second biscuit. Some invisible benefactor loves you, strangely, and you have no idea who.`}]},{id:`cof_cookie_2b`,title:`The Perfect Moment`,reqStory:`path_cookie_save`,text:`You have your fresh coffee in your hand. It is steaming. Then you remember the biscuit in your pocket. You get it out. The chocolate has softened a little from your body heat.`,opts:[{t:`Dunk it and enjoy`,m:10,l:5,a:-25,b:0,r:`You dunk the biscuit briefly in the hot coffee. It melts on your tongue. An explosion of caramel and roasted notes. For one moment the world is perfect.`},{t:`Improvise a crumb topping`,m:5,l:5,a:-15,b:0,r:`You crumble the biscuit over the milk foam. Gourmet coffee, home-built. Somewhere in Italy a barista is weeping; here it tastes magnificent.`}]},{id:`cof_disaster_1`,title:`OUT OF ORDER`,text:`You need caffeine. Urgently. And all the display on the machine says is: 'ERROR 418 - I'm a teapot'. Your hands are shaking slightly already.`,opts:[{t:`Repair it`,req:`screw`,next:`path_machine_love`,m:15,l:0,a:-10,b:-5,r:`You unscrew the panel and secure the hose. The machine hums gratefully! The first sip tastes of victory (and a little limescale).`},{t:`Pop the bubble wrap therapeutically`,req:`bubble_wrap`,next:`path_machine_confused`,m:10,l:5,a:-15,b:0,r:`You sit down on the floor and pop wrap until the shaking stops. *Pop. Pop.* No coffee, and no murder either.`},{t:`Give it a kick`,next:`path_machine_war`,m:5,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`BAM! You kick the casing. A gush of hot water runs over your shoes. The machine beeps angrily.`}]},{id:`cof_disaster_2a`,title:`The Machine's Revenge`,reqStory:`path_machine_war`,text:`You come back. The display is glowing red. The text runs past as a ticker, because it is so long: 'ERROR 418.666.KICK_DETECTED.USER_BLACKLISTED.SELF_DEFENSE_MODE_ACTIVE.38472.DO_NOT_TOUCH'. There is a smell of burning.`,opts:[{t:`Pull the plug and end the war`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:10,r:`You pull the plug. The red light dies slowly, like the eye of HAL 9000. The war is yours... for now.`},{t:`Approach cautiously`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`The machine spits out boiling steam without warning. As though it had been waiting for you! You back away. The thing is malevolent.`}]},{id:`cof_disaster_2b`,title:`System Overload`,reqStory:`path_machine_love`,text:`The machine is blinking wildly in every colour. Error code: 'ERROR 200.OK.BUT.HEARTBEAT.OVERFLOW.999999.USER_IS_MY_HERO.CALC_LOVE.DIV_BY_ZERO'. It seems so excited about your return that it crashes.`,opts:[{t:`Talk it down: 'Steady now, girl'`,m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You stroke the casing. The blinking slows. She brews you a 'special espresso' with double crema. It tastes of affection.`},{t:`Give it one firm thump`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Old school. The machine takes offence and reverts to default settings. The coffee is fine; the magic has gone.`}]},{id:`cof_disaster_2c`,title:`A Philosophical Error`,reqStory:`path_machine_confused`,text:`The display now shows columns of figures: 'ERROR 503.PLOPP.UNDEFINED.WHAT_IS_PURPOSE.BUBBLE_LOGIC_EXCEPTION.7463.8291.000'. The machine is apparently trying to calculate the purpose of your bubble wrap episode.`,opts:[{t:`Pop back`,req:`bubble_wrap`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You pop one bubble. The machine beeps once. You pop again. It beeps twice. A level of mutual understanding has been reached.`},{t:`Ignore it`,m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You leave it calculating. Let it work out pi, as long as it produces coffee again at some point.`}]},{id:`cof_sugar_1`,title:`The Sugar Baron`,text:`You hear frantic rustling. Bernd (Sales) is bent over in front of the supply cupboard. His suit pockets are bulging suspiciously. He is sweating. 'Pssst! That lot upstairs want to rationalise! The Great Reset is coming! I am securing the white gold!' He stares at you wildly. 'Are you in, or are you a sheep?'`,opts:[{t:`'I am telling the boss.'`,next:`path_sugar_embargo`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`Bernd's eyes narrow to slits. 'You will be sorry. When the crisis comes, you will come crawling!' He disappears into the shadows of the copier room. You have made yourself a powerful enemy.`},{t:`'What does a gram go for?'`,next:`path_sugar_dealer`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Bernd produces a calculator. 'The daily price fluctuates. But for you... swap for staples?' You haggle briefly. You let him carry on.`},{t:`'Give me 20 per cent!'`,next:`path_sugar_junkie`,m:5,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Bernd grins broadly (a gold tooth flashes). 'Good man. Diversification is everything.' He shovels three handfuls of sachets into your pocket. You nod at each other conspiratorially. The cartel is established.`}]},{id:`cof_sugar_2a`,title:`The Margin Call`,reqStory:`path_sugar_junkie`,text:`Bernd heads you off. He is practically vibrating. His pupils are enormous and there are white crumbs stuck all round his mouth. 'The market has crashed! I used it all myself! I need my stake back! Have you got the gear?!'`,opts:[{t:`Drive the price up`,m:10,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`'Supply and demand, Bernd.' You demand the armrests off his office chair in exchange. He whimpers and agrees. The new baron has taken office.`},{t:`Give him the sugar back`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`You give him the sachets. He tears three open at once and tips them straight down his throat. 'Ohhh yes... Mummy is home.' He goes quiet immediately and slides down the wall. Crisis averted.`}]},{id:`cof_sugar_2b`,title:`The Embargo`,reqStory:`path_sugar_embargo`,text:`Coffee there is. The sugar bowl is empty. Stuck to it instead is a note: 'Temporarily out of service owing to supply chain problems. Signed, Bernd'. Bernd is sitting three desks away on a throne of copier paper, grinning at you nastily.`,opts:[{t:`Storm the bunker`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:10,r:`You throw yourself at his paper tower. Bernd squeaks. Sugar sachets rain through the office like confetti. Colleagues cheer and join in the looting. The revolution has succeeded!`},{t:`Surrender and beg`,m:5,l:-10,a:20,b:0,r:`You grovel. 'Please, Bernd. Just one spoonful.' He flicks a single crumb at you. 'That will be €5 handling fee.' It is humiliating.`}]},{id:`cof_sugar_2c`,title:`Black Market`,reqStory:`path_sugar_dealer`,text:`The corridor is bustling. Bernd has set up a small stall. He sells sugar for pens, Post-its and canteen vouchers. Business is booming.`,opts:[{t:`Go to the boss and spill it`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:10,r:`The boss comes, sees the operation... and buys two sachets himself for his meeting. 'Out of petty cash, Bernd.' Your faith in the system is gone.`},{t:`Hire on as security`,m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:0,r:`You fold your arms and look menacing so that nobody steals anything. Bernd cuts you in on the profit (two highlighters). A lucrative sideline.`}]},{id:`cof_mold_1`,title:`Fridge Expedition`,text:`Right at the back of the fridge stands a yoghurt. The use-by date is 'May 2012'. It pulses faintly in neon green. As you approach, furry letters form on its surface: 'H...U...N...G...E...R'.`,opts:[{t:`Slam the door and flee`,next:`path_mold_civ`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Out of sight, out of mind. You stick an 'OUT OF ORDER' note on the fridge. Let the night shift wrestle with the new life form.`},{t:`Sacrifice a sugar sachet to it`,next:`path_mold_ally`,m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You sprinkle sugar in. The fungus absorbs it happily and burps quietly. A squeaky voice in your head says: 'WE SERVE THE MASTER.' A revolting friend has entered your life.`},{t:`Attack it with disinfectant`,next:`path_mold_war`,m:10,l:5,a:15,b:0,r:`You spray Sagrotan. The fungus hisses aggressively, like a cat! It retreats, and you can hear it giggling in the drain. This is not over.`}]},{id:`cof_mold_2a`,title:`The Symbiosis`,reqStory:`path_mold_ally`,text:`You open the fridge again. The yoghurt has grown. 'MASTER', it squeaks. 'THE ENEMY (BOSS) HAS STORED HIS SANDWICH IN HERE. SHALL WE... OPTIMISE IT FOR FLAVOUR?'`,opts:[{t:`Decline politely and keep the peace`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'AS YOU WISH.' The fungus seems disappointed, and forms a little heart for you anyway. It is sweet, and also profoundly revolting.`},{t:`Give the order: 'Go!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:10,a:-20,b:20,r:`The fungus wobbles cheerfully over to the sandwich. Later you hear the boss bellowing: 'Why does my bread taste of blueberry and revenge?!'. You grin nastily.`}]},{id:`cof_mold_2b`,title:`Spore Alert`,reqStory:`path_mold_war`,text:`You go to get milk, and the yoghurt has built a trap! The moment the light comes on, a cloud of green spores shoots straight into your face. It is defending its territory!`,opts:[{t:`Cough and weep`,m:10,l:-5,a:20,b:0,r:`You cough your soul out. Your eyes burn. The yoghurt appears to be laughing scornfully. You have lost a fight against a dairy product.`},{t:`Combine deodorant and lighter into a flamethrower`,m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`You burn the shelf out. The stench is bestial and the enemy is annihilated. The caretaker will ask questions; the field is yours.`}]},{id:`cof_mold_2c`,title:`The Civilisation`,reqStory:`path_mold_civ`,text:`You risk a look. Things have moved on in the salad drawer. The fungus has built little houses out of old cheese. Tiny fungus men ride on cockroaches. They have invented the wheel.`,opts:[{t:`Play God with the fridge light`,m:20,l:0,a:-15,b:0,r:`You switch the fridge light on and off. The little creatures fall to their knees and worship you. 'THE LIGHT-BRINGER!'. Your ego enjoys this.`},{t:`Sweep the lot into the bin`,m:5,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You end their history brutally with a bin bag. An entire universe, annihilated in seconds. A brief pang of guilt, and then you fetch your milk.`}]},{id:`cof_catering_1`,title:`The Leftovers of Power`,text:`The management meeting is over. The remains are standing on the mahogany table. Salmon rolls, caviar canapés, premium coffee. Nobody in sight.`,opts:[{t:`Clear up dutifully`,next:`path_cat_cleanup`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:15,l:-15,a:5,b:-5,r:`You clear plates away. Under the boss's chair you find a piece of paper: 'TOP SECRET: list of staff we want to fire'. Your name is not on it... not yet.`},{t:`Greedily eat the lot`,next:`path_cat_eat`,m:10,l:15,a:-15,b:0,r:`You stuff yourself like a hamster. Salmon, grapes, cheese. For ten minutes you live like the board. Unfortunately there is a fat tartare sauce stain on your shirt now.`},{t:`Steal only the coffee`,next:`path_cat_gossip`,m:5,l:-10,a:-5,b:0,r:`You fill your cup with the good 'Arabica Gold'. Sabine from Reception heads you off at the door. She grins knowingly. She saw you.`}]},{id:`cof_catering_2a`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Delicate Information`,reqStory:`path_cat_cleanup`,text:`The boss comes back in a hurry. He is looking for that exact piece of paper. He looks at you, panic in his eyes. 'Miller! Have you seen any... paperwork in here?'`,opts:[{t:`'Here it is, sir.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:5,l:0,a:15,b:10,r:`He snatches it out of your hand. Instead of gratitude there is coldness. He knows now that YOU know. 'Forget that. Immediately.' You are on his watch list from this point on.`},{t:`Simply eat the paper`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":2},m:5,l:5,a:-20,b:-20,r:`You look him in the eye, put the paper in your mouth and swallow it. 'I saw nothing, sir.' He nods slowly, deeply impressed. 'Good man. Loyalty tastes bitter, does it not?'`}]},{id:`cof_catering_2b`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Burden of Proof`,reqStory:`path_cat_eat`,text:`You walk straight into the boss. He stares at the enormous grease stain on your shirt and the crumbs at the corner of your mouth. 'Miller? Have you been eating from the board's buffet?'`,opts:[{t:`'I ate my packed lunch.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You point at the stain. 'Liver sausage, sir. Nasty stuff.' He wrinkles his nose and keeps his distance. 'Go and wash. You smell of fish.' You have escaped.`},{t:`'It had to go, it would only spoil!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:20,r:`'That is €50 salmon, Miller! It is not dog food!' He is livid at the disrespect. That earns a written warning for helping yourself.`}]},{id:`cof_catering_2c`,title:`A 'Small' Favour`,reqStory:`path_cat_gossip`,text:`Sabine blocks the way. 'I will not tell anybody about the coffee... but my printer is making these odd noises. Could you take a *really quick* look? Please!'`,opts:[{t:`'Oh God! Is that a spider?!'`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You point behind her in a panic. Sabine shrieks and jumps aside. You use the chaos and run. Not elegant; effective.`},{t:`Swallow the blackmail and help`,m:45,l:-15,a:25,b:-15,r:`A classic mistake. It was not the printer, it was the driver. And the network. You are trapped for 45 minutes. Sabine tells you her entire life story while you work. You hate yourself.`}]},{id:`cof_bulletin_board`,title:`Waiting for the Black Gold`,text:`The machine's progress bar has been stuck at 99% for what feels like an eternity. A single drop falls in slow motion. The suspense is almost unbearable.`,opts:[{t:`Kill the time with Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:5,r:`Kevin talks at you at length about his 'gaming rug'. It is dreadful, and at the end of it you are holding a fresh, hot coffee.`},{t:`Fidget impatiently and run back`,m:2,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You cannot take any more and snatch the cup away. A hot drop lands on your shirt, and you are back at your desk immediately.`},{t:`Study the 'noticeboard'`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`CMD:OPEN_BOARD`}]},{id:`cof_lore_2c`,char:`Kevin`,title:`The Rumour Mill`,reqStory:`path_lore_ignore`,text:`You run into Kevin in the kitchen. He grins broadly and waves a ring binder about. 'Guess what I found in the server room? The HR list! I am going to blackmail everybody!'`,opts:[{t:`Report him to the boss`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":10,Kevin:-20},m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:-15,r:`You ring Dr Wichtig. Shortly afterwards Kevin is led away by two security men. Your standing with the boss has risen.`},{t:`Warn him`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Kevin, HR are looking for that. Burn it.' He goes pale. 'Oh... cheers, bro.' He runs to the shredder.`},{t:`Ignore it`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Not your problem. 10 minutes later you hear screaming from the HR office. Well, then.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_hack_1`,char:`Kevin`,title:`Kevin's Upgrade`,text:`Kevin has unscrewed the rear panel of the coffee machine and soldered a Raspberry Pi onto the board. 'I am installing Doom on the display. And I have overclocked the water temperature to 105 degrees. Do you want to do the first test run?'`,opts:[{t:`'I am having... tea today.'`,next:`path_kevin_hack_ignore`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You leave the kitchen before anybody can identify you as an accomplice.`},{t:`'Put that back the way it was, now!'`,next:`path_kevin_hack_stop`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:10,l:-5,a:5,b:-5,r:`You make him disconnect the cables. Kevin grumbles: 'Innovation really does get held back around here.' The machine looks normal again.`},{t:`'Can it mine Bitcoin as well?'`,next:`path_kevin_hack_help`,rep:{Kevin:10},m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:10,r:`Kevin practically glows. 'Good idea! I will divert the power from the fridge.' You tinker on together for a bit. There is a faint smell of scorched plastic.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_hack_2a`,title:`Lukewarm Dishwater`,reqStory:`path_kevin_hack_stop`,text:`The coffee machine blinks green: 'SAFE MODE'. The coffee comes out at exactly 60 degrees and tastes watery. Kevin has activated the economy settings out of spite.`,opts:[{t:`Drink it and suffer`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`It tastes of compromise and sadness. Your caffeine level barely moves.`},{t:`Go and find Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-2},m:5,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You do not find him. He is presumably hiding in Stores. You stay tired.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_hack_2b`,title:`Meltdown`,reqStory:`path_kevin_hack_help`,text:`As you step into the kitchen the coffee machine is glowing dark red. Doom is genuinely running on the display, and the coffee has evaporated. The whole room is a sauna.`,opts:[{t:`Pull the plug`,m:5,l:-5,a:0,b:0,r:`You save the building. The machine dies with a sad little whine. No coffee today.`},{t:`Warm yourself in front of it`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`Warm, if nothing else. You enjoy the tropical heat until the smoke alarm goes off.`}]},{id:`cof_kevin_hack_2c`,title:`Blue Screen`,reqStory:`path_kevin_hack_ignore`,text:`The coffee machine is showing a Blue Screen of Death: 'Error 404: Beans not found'. Kevin is standing next to it scratching his head. 'I think I have fried the mainboard.'`,opts:[{t:`Laugh`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Well, then. Not my problem.' You go without coffee and with a warm sense of schadenfreude.`},{t:`Call Egon`,rep:{Egon:5},m:5,l:-5,a:0,b:0,r:`You grass Kevin up to the caretaker. Egon arrives with the big pipe wrench. This is going to be loud.`}]},{id:`cof_chantal_tiktok_1`,char:`Chantal`,title:`Content Creation`,text:`Chantal has set up a ring light in front of the coffee machine. 'Hey! Can you film for a second? I am doing the 'no sleep challenge'. I have to look as though I am inhaling the coffee. Be aesthetic!'`,opts:[{t:`'Sure, action!'`,next:`path_chantal_tiktok_help`,rep:{Chantal:10},m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You film 15 takes. 'More drama!' she calls. The coffee ends up cold and Chantal ends up happy.`},{t:`Pull the plug on the sly`,next:`path_chantal_tiktok_ruin`,rep:{Chantal:-15},m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`The light goes out mid-take. 'My vibe!' she screams. You shrug. 'Power cut.'`},{t:`Push her aside`,next:`path_chantal_tiktok_push`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You barge through the set-up. Chantal films your back. 'And here we see negative energy in the wild.'`}]},{id:`cof_chantal_tiktok_2a`,char:`Chantal`,title:`A Thank-You`,reqStory:`path_chantal_tiktok_help`,text:`Chantal heads you off. 'The video has 300 views! Here, as a thank-you.' She presses a cup of green liquid into your hand. 'Detox spinach matcha latte. Home-made.'`,opts:[{t:`Tip it into the plant`,rep:{Chantal:-2},m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`The ficus drops its leaves immediately. You have spared the office a biological weapon.`},{t:`Bravely drink the cup dry`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`It tastes of meadow and soil. You gag it down. Chantal beams. 'Can you sense the glow?'`}]},{id:`cof_chantal_tiktok_2b`,title:`Cancel Culture`,reqStory:`path_chantal_tiktok_ruin`,text:`You come into the kitchen. Above the coffee machine hangs a printed screenshot of your face, crossed out in red. Underneath it says: 'Warning: energy vampire'.`,opts:[{t:`Tear it down`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You screw the note up. It has the shape of a small victory, and the war has only just started.`},{t:`Laugh about it`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You draw yourself a moustache on the picture. Chantal sees it later and is confused.`}]},{id:`cof_chantal_tiktok_2c`,title:`Passive-Aggressive`,reqStory:`path_chantal_tiktok_push`,text:`The coffee machine is plastered with pink Post-its. 'Please keep your distance!', 'Positive Vibes Only!', 'No rushing!'. It takes you 2 minutes to uncover the start button.`,opts:[{t:`Tear the lot off`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You make one large ball of paper. That was satisfying.`},{t:`Press for coffee blind`,m:2,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You press through the paper. It was the button for 'Hot Water'. Your coffee is ruined.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_trap_1`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Honey Trap`,text:`Dr Wichtig is standing at the machine, smiling. He is holding two cups. 'Ah, Miller! Perfect timing. I am feeling generous today. Would you like this double espresso? From my private supply. On the house.'`,opts:[{t:`'Is there poison in it?'`,next:`path_ceo_trap_doubt`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:5,r:`His smile sets. 'Your sense of humour is... particular, Miller. It is only coffee. Or do you have a guilty conscience?'`},{t:`Accept gratefully: 'Wow, thank you, sir!'`,next:`path_ceo_trap_taken`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:5,l:-5,a:-5,b:-5,r:`You take the cup. It is hot and smells glorious. The boss smiles more broadly. 'Wonderful. Anybody with time for pleasure is bound to have energy to spare.'`},{t:`'I have urgent work.'`,next:`path_ceo_trap_denied`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":10},m:2,l:-10,a:5,b:-10,r:`You wave it away and hurry on. The boss nods his approval. 'Discipline! I like that. Carry on!'`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_trap_2a`,title:`The Receipt`,reqStory:`path_ceo_trap_taken`,text:`Back at your desk an enormous stack of unsorted invoices is waiting. A Post-it is stuck to it: 'Since you are freshly fortified – please work through these by 17:00. Thank you for the coffee chat. Dr W.'`,opts:[{t:`Slide the stack over to Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-10},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`You put the stack on Kevin's desk without drawing attention. He will not notice until it is too late.`},{t:`Work through the stack yourself`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:45,l:-20,a:20,b:0,r:`You sort invoices by date, then by amount, then by date again, because the Post-it does not say which. Three quarters of an hour later the pile is in order. The coffee was good; the price was too high.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_trap_2b`,char:`Markus`,title:`Collateral Damage`,reqStory:`path_ceo_trap_denied`,text:`You see Markus in the corridor. He is hauling heavy archive boxes and sweating. 'The boss caught me', he pants. 'He said anybody with time for coffee has time for lifting. If only I had said no...'`,opts:[{t:`Grin with schadenfreude`,m:2,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`The suffering of others is the finest consolation. You did everything right.`},{t:`Laugh at Markus`,rep:{Markus:-10},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You go over briefly to laugh at Markus. 'Beginner's mistake', you whisper.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_trap_2c`,title:`HR Review`,reqStory:`path_ceo_trap_doubt`,text:`An email from HR pops up. 'Routine loyalty review'. Dr Wichtig has evidently reported your scepticism as 'lack of trust in the leadership level'.`,opts:[{t:`Panic`,m:10,l:0,a:10,b:10,r:`You frantically delete your browser history and hide your personal snacks. The paranoia rises.`},{t:`Stay cool`,m:5,l:0,a:0,b:5,r:`You fill the questionnaire in with stock phrases. 'I love this company.' Hopefully that will do.`}]},{id:`cof_egon_fix_1`,char:`Egon`,title:`Open Surgery`,text:`The coffee machine is in pieces. Egon is poking about in the grinder with a screwdriver. 'Limescale. Limescale everywhere. And somebody has dropped chewing gum in. That has to be solved mechanically.'`,opts:[{t:`'Why not simply use descaler.'`,next:`path_egon_fix_chem`,rep:{Egon:-10},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Egon glares at you. 'Chemicals are for softies! This is precision work.' He hammers angrily at the tank.`},{t:`Pay him to make it faster`,next:`path_egon_fix_turbo`,rep:{Egon:5},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You slip him a chocolate bar. 'Can you raise the pressure?' Egon grins. 'I will take the safety screw out. At your own risk.'`},{t:`Hold the parts`,next:`path_egon_fix_help`,rep:{Egon:10},m:20,l:-10,a:10,b:0,r:`You hold the flap, the torch and your tongue. Egon grunts contentedly. 'You have hands that can work. Rare, round here.'`}]},{id:`cof_egon_fix_2a`,title:`Cold Coffee`,reqStory:`path_egon_fix_chem`,text:`At the next attempt the machine does run again, and Egon has disconnected the heating element out of spite. The coffee comes out at exactly 18 degrees.`,opts:[{t:`Use the microwave`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You warm the coffee up in the microwave. It now tastes of burnt plastic and limescale.`},{t:`Complain`,rep:{Egon:-5},m:5,l:0,a:20,b:0,r:`You find a note: 'Complaints in writing to the caretaker's basement, level -3.' Somewhere out of sight he gives a dirty laugh.`}]},{id:`cof_egon_fix_2b`,title:`Palpitations`,reqStory:`path_egon_fix_turbo`,text:`The coffee does not flow, it fires into the cup. It is as black as crude oil and has the consistency of syrup. The cup vibrates faintly on the saucer.`,opts:[{t:`Sip cautiously`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Far too strong. You get heartburn on the spot. Egon calls from a distance: 'That is diesel for the soul!'`},{t:`Down it in one`,m:5,l:-20,a:10,b:0,r:`You drink it. Your pupils dilate. You can suddenly see sounds. You work at 300% speed for the next 2 hours.`}]},{id:`cof_egon_fix_2c`,char:`Egon`,title:`A Tradesman's Honour`,reqStory:`path_egon_fix_help`,text:`The machine purrs like a kitten. Egon is standing in the corridor and nods to you. He has hung a 'Reserved' sign on the machine for you.`,opts:[{t:`Thank him and enjoy it`,rep:{Egon:5},m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`The best coffee in weeks. And you have the respect of the caretaker. It does not pay a rise, and it opens doors. Literally.`},{t:`Remove the sign`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You do not want special treatment. The coffee tastes good all the same.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_audit_1`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`The Budget Check`,text:`Ms Elster is at the coffee machine with a clipboard. She notes down every cup. 'Mr Miller! Bean consumption is up 4.2% in Q3. Have you filled in withdrawal form K-7?'`,opts:[{t:`Put a euro in the box`,next:`path_elster_audit_pay`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`Her look softens. 'A donation? Most commendable. We will book that under 'Other income'. Carry on.'`},{t:`'I only take hot water.'`,next:`path_elster_audit_lie`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`She nods, satisfied. 'Exemplary! Water is free and good for the balance sheet. Drink up!'`},{t:`'Coffee is a basic right!'`,next:`path_elster_audit_fight`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-10},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`She purses her lipstick. 'Basic rights cost money. I am noting: uncooperative conduct regarding resource allocation.'`}]},{id:`cof_elster_audit_2a`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`Rationing`,reqStory:`path_elster_audit_fight`,text:`You head for the machine. The display shows: 'LIMIT REACHED'. A note from Ms Elster hangs beside it: 'Owing to wastefulness, the IT department has been throttled to 2 cups a day.'`,opts:[{t:`Kick the machine in a rage`,m:2,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`It achieves nothing except a hurting toe. The machine remains obstinate.`},{t:`Scrounge off marketing`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:10,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You sneak over to Chantal's Nespresso machine. She catches you. 'That costs extra, mind!'`}]},{id:`cof_elster_audit_2b`,title:`The Paper War`,reqStory:`path_elster_audit_pay`,text:`An envelope is waiting at your place. Contents: a donation receipt for €1.00 and a two-page form for the 'fiscal recording of minimal amounts', which you have to sign.`,opts:[{t:`Fill it in`,rep:{"Frau Elster":2},m:15,l:-10,a:5,b:0,r:`You waste 15 minutes of working time on €1. Ms Elster is happy, your soul weeps.`},{t:`Ignore it`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-5},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`The form goes in the bin. You know she will record it on her blacklist.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_audit_2c`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`Compulsory Tea`,reqStory:`path_elster_audit_lie`,text:`Ms Elster is lying in wait for you again. 'Mr Miller! I saw you squinting in the direction of the coffee beans. Let us stay with our healthy water, shall we?' She watches you sternly.`,opts:[{t:`Pull a coffee on the sly`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-10},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You wait until she blinks and press 'Espresso' quickly. It tastes of freedom with a note of criminal offence.`},{t:`Obediently drink water`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You drink hot water. It tastes of nothing. Your caffeine withdrawal begins.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_pitch_1`,char:`Markus`,title:`Networking`,text:`Markus heads you off. He is leaning casually against the machine, blocking the spout. 'Miller! Coffee is for closers. Speaking of which... have you ever thought about passive income? Crypto? NFTs of bored cats? I could bring you into the inner circle.'`,opts:[{t:`Feign interest - there might be free coffee in it`,next:`path_markus_pitch_scam`,rep:{Markus:5},m:15,l:10,a:-5,b:0,r:`He talks for 15 minutes about blockchain and mindset. You understood none of it, and he pays for your coffee with his 'Black Card'.`},{t:`'Is this a pyramid scheme?'`,next:`path_markus_pitch_hate`,rep:{Markus:-10},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Markus goes red. 'It is multi-level marketing! You simply have the mindset of an employee.' He storms off, offended.`},{t:`Say nothing and stare`,next:`path_markus_pitch_alpha`,rep:{Markus:5},m:2,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`You look him in the eye without a word, press the button and go. Markus nods respectfully. 'Alpha move. I like it.'`}]},{id:`cof_markus_pitch_2a`,title:`Spam Attack`,reqStory:`path_markus_pitch_scam`,text:`Your inbox is overflowing. Markus has signed you up to his newsletter 'Porsche in 3 weeks' without asking. Subject: 'WAKE UP MATRIX SLAVE!!!'.`,opts:[{t:`Confront Markus`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'That is growth hacking!' he says in his defence. Your temples throb in time with his buzzwords.`},{t:`Delete and block`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You spend time building filters. The WhatsApp messages keep coming regardless.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_pitch_2b`,char:`Markus`,title:`Character Assassination`,reqStory:`path_markus_pitch_hate`,text:`You hear Markus bad-mouthing you in the kitchen. 'Miller? Total low performer. Holds up revenue. Afraid of success.' Gabi and Chantal are listening.`,opts:[{t:`Wade in`,rep:{Markus:-5,Gabi:5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You show him up. 'How are your NFTs doing, Markus?' Silence. Gabi giggles.`},{t:`Ignore it`,m:2,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You breathe the anger away. The lion does not concern himself with the opinion of sheep.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_pitch_2c`,char:`Markus`,title:`The Mentor`,reqStory:`path_markus_pitch_alpha`,text:`Markus comes over to your desk. He puts a book down in front of you: 'The 4-Hour Workweek'. 'For you, tiger. We wolves have to stick together.'`,opts:[{t:`Actually read some of it`,rep:{Markus:5},m:30,l:20,a:5,b:0,r:`You read three pages. The entire point of it is outsourcing work to other people. You need a wash.`},{t:`Use the book as a monitor stand`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`It is exactly the right height. Neck pain gone at last. Thanks, Markus.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_break_1`,char:`Gabi`,title:`Hide and Seek`,text:`Gabi is crouching behind the big pot plant beside the coffee machine. She whispers: 'Pssst! I am hiding from the UPS man. He has a parcel that weighs 30kg. Say nothing!'`,opts:[{t:`'SHE IS OVER THERE!'`,next:`path_gabi_break_snitch`,rep:{Gabi:-10},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:-5,r:`Gabi has to crawl out of her hiding place. Her look could kill while she signs for the parcel.`},{t:`'Have not seen her.'`,next:`path_gabi_break_help`,rep:{Gabi:10},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`The courier withdraws. Gabi breathes out. 'You are a lifesaver. Have a biscuit.'`},{t:`'That will cost you a coffee.'`,next:`path_gabi_break_deal`,rep:{Gabi:-5},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`She rolls her eyes and buys you one from the machine anyway. 'Greedy sod. A deal is a deal, though.'`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_break_2a`,char:`Gabi`,title:`Postal Revenge`,reqStory:`path_gabi_break_snitch`,text:`You are waiting for an urgent parcel. Gabi grins at you from Reception. 'Oh, that? I sent that back. 'Addressee gone away'. Well, then. Bad luck.'`,opts:[{t:`Drive to the depot`,m:45,l:-20,a:10,b:0,r:`You drive to the depot, stand behind three people with returns and show ID to collect a parcel with 'Addressee gone away' stuck on it. That cost you nearly an hour, and Gabi had counted on every minute of it.`},{t:`Lose it`,rep:{Gabi:-5},m:10,l:0,a:20,b:0,r:`You shout. Gabi is filing her nails. 'Your aggression is in breach of the house rules.'`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_break_2b`,char:`Gabi`,title:`Early Warning System`,reqStory:`path_gabi_break_help`,text:`Your phone rings once, briefly, just as you were about to stand up. Gabi: 'Code red. Dr Wichtig is on his way to you. He looks cross. Look busy.'`,opts:[{t:`Flee`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You are gone before he arrives. The door swings shut and his shadow appears in the frosted glass. It does not get closer than that.`},{t:`Prepare`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-2},m:5,l:-10,a:5,b:-10,r:`By the time the boss arrives you are buried deep in Excel. He nods with satisfaction and moves on. Gabi has saved you.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_break_2c`,char:`Gabi`,title:`Settling Debts`,reqStory:`path_gabi_break_deal`,text:`Gabi slams a chocolate bar down on your desk. 'There. Your hush money. I hope it tastes of betrayal.'`,opts:[{t:`Apologise`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`'It was only a joke.' Gabi grunts something that distantly resembles reconciliation and pushes the bar closer to you. 'Yes, yes. Eat it.' The row is officially adjourned.`},{t:`Eat it`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`It tastes of chocolate. Morals are for people who are not hungry.`}]},{id:`cof_descale_absurd_1`,title:`Descaling: Step 1 of 73`,text:`You need coffee. The machine blocks you: 'DESCALING REQUIRED'. The on-screen assistant demands the absurd: 'Step 1: tilt the water tank 45 degrees. Step 2: open the drawer 3x.' The boss calls out as he passes: 'Good of you to get on with it! Stick with it!'`,opts:[{t:`Bridge the sensor manually`,req:`screw`,next:`path_descale_screw`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You use the screwdriver to press the hidden microswitch for 'cleaning complete'. The stupid machine believes you. The coffee runs. You go back to the office, content.`},{t:`Just tip vinegar essence in`,next:`path_descale_vinegar`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:0,r:`You tip neat vinegar into the tank and start the rinse cycle blind. It takes a while and you have no patience for waiting. You slip quietly away to your office.`},{t:`Carry out all 73 steps`,next:`path_descale_brav`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":10},m:75,l:-10,a:30,b:-5,r:`Seventy-five minutes! You had to massage the steam wand with a toothbrush. Your mood is at zero. The boss is happy. You have no appetite for coffee at all now and go back to work.`}]},{id:`cof_descale_absurd_2a`,title:`The Coffee God`,reqStory:`path_descale_brav`,text:`You have recovered from the 75-minute trauma and step into the kitchen. The machine is so clean it gleams like a diamond. Nobody else has dared use it yet.`,opts:[{t:`Reverently draw the first coffee`,m:10,l:10,a:-20,b:0,r:`Your first drawn coffee is a revelation. Perfect crema, perfect temperature. This coffee heals wounds. With the first sip, the seventy-five minutes with the toothbrush are paid in full.`},{t:`Put an 'Out of Service' sign on it`,m:5,l:5,a:10,b:10,r:`You reserve the clean machine for yourself alone. Colleagues are livid and complain to the boss. Your coffee stays pure from then on.`},{t:`Sell the coffee to Chantal for €5`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`You sell the perfect 'first brew' to the caffeine-addicted Chantal. She pays, grumbling. You are rich and she hates your capitalism.`}]},{id:`cof_descale_absurd_2b`,char:`Markus`,title:`Lumps in the Cup`,reqStory:`path_descale_screw`,text:`Hours after your screwdriver episode, Markus from Sales brings a cup to your office. He very nearly spits. 'Tell me, what is wrong with the coffee?! There are little white lumps floating in it! Is that cocaine or poison?!'`,opts:[{t:`Feel guilty and fetch him a fresh coffee from the bakery`,m:20,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You go out and buy him a decent coffee. He is mollified, and you are down 20 minutes and €3.`},{t:`'That is vanilla flavour crunch!'`,rep:{Markus:5},m:5,l:0,a:0,b:0,r:`Markus stares into the cup. 'Crunch? Oh, premium!' He genuinely drinks it down. The limescale problem has resolved itself.`},{t:`'Then descale it yourself!'`,rep:{Markus:-10},m:5,l:0,a:10,b:5,r:`Markus throws the coffee angrily into your bin. 'Always the same arrogant IT!' A friend lost, time saved.`}]},{id:`cof_descale_absurd_2c`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`Salad Dressing`,reqStory:`path_descale_vinegar`,text:`Some time passes. Then the door of the boss's office flies open. He is gagging. 'Miller! What is in the coffee machine?! I wanted an espresso and it tastes like lukewarm cucumber salad! The entire corridor smells of vinegar!'`,opts:[{t:`'Phone is ringing, must dash!'`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:10,r:`You run back to your office in a panic and lock the door. The boss carries on bellowing in the corridor and finds himself another victim. Cowardly; effective.`},{t:`'It must be an act of sabotage!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:10,l:0,a:15,b:15,r:`The boss half believes you, and sentences you to flush the machine with clean water for 30 minutes. The botch job from earlier has caught up with you.`},{t:`'It is a life hack off the internet!'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-15},m:5,l:0,a:20,b:30,r:`The boss goes red. 'Keep your life hacks out of my machine!' He is beside himself and bellows at you the length of the corridor.`}]},{id:`cof_swiss_choc_1`,title:`The Sweet Find`,text:`Somebody has left a sinfully expensive, still-sealed bar of fine Swiss chocolate on top of the microwave. No note, no name. It is simply lying there, calling your name.`,opts:[{t:`Impound it as IT lost property`,loot:`chocolate`,next:`path_choc_steal`,m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You make the chocolate disappear into your bag, professionally. Nobody saw anything. An excellent haul.`},{t:`Add a Post-it: 'For everybody?'`,next:`path_choc_share`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You are a social animal. You stick a note on it. We shall see how long that lasts.`},{t:`Ignore it. Bound to be a trap.`,next:`path_choc_ignore`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`That is bound to be a social experiment from HR. You make your coffee and disappear.`}]},{id:`cof_swiss_choc_2a`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`The Confectionery Thief`,reqStory:`path_choc_steal`,text:`Ms Elster hangs a tearful note on the kitchen door: 'Who has stolen my diet-exception chocolate? I am deeply disappointed in this team!'`,opts:[{t:`Feign sympathy`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You read the note and shake your head theatrically at such barefaced cheek. The chocolate in your backpack, or your stomach, weighs a great deal all of a sudden.`},{t:`Blame the cleaner`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`'It was probably the cleaning contractor', you whisper to her. She nods angrily. Abysmal karma; you are in the clear.`}]},{id:`cof_swiss_choc_2b`,title:`Feeding Time at the Zoo`,reqStory:`path_choc_share`,text:`Your note 'For everybody?' has caused a bloodbath. The bar was gone in seconds. Kevin the apprentice has stomach ache, because he ate nearly all of it himself. Ms Elster is hunting furiously for her chocolate.`,opts:[{t:`Defend Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:5,"Frau Elster":-5},m:5,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`'If you do not write your name on it, that is your own fault!' you say, blocking. Kevin looks at you the way you look at a superhero.`},{t:`Grass Kevin up loudly`,rep:{Kevin:-5,"Frau Elster":5},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You direct Ms Elster's wrath elegantly onto Kevin. He has to stand in the corner and be ashamed. You wash your hands in innocence.`}]},{id:`cof_swiss_choc_2c`,title:`Use-By Date`,reqStory:`path_choc_ignore`,text:`The chocolate lay untouched on the microwave for three days. By now it has melted and gone hard again. Egon is scraping the brown patch off, irritated.`,opts:[{t:`Pitch in and scrape`,rep:{Egon:10},m:10,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You fetch a scraper and help him. Cleaning together forges a bond.`},{t:`Praise Egon for his cleaning`,rep:{Egon:5},m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`'Good work, Egon.' He only grumbles something unintelligible back, and deep down he is pleased.`}]},{id:`cof_stolen_sandwich_1`,title:`Fridge Mafia`,text:`You open the fridge for some milk. Inside, a perfectly made pastrami sandwich smiles up at you. Stuck to it is a passive-aggressive note: 'Hands off! Property of Markus (Sales)!!!'`,opts:[{t:`Confiscate the sandwich`,loot:`sandwich`,next:`path_sandwich_steal`,m:2,l:-5,a:0,b:5,r:`Sales earn too much anyway. You take the sandwich. It is part of the IT infrastructure now.`},{t:`Only swap the note`,next:`path_sandwich_prank`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You cross out 'Markus' and write 'Egon' on it. This is going to be extremely funny before the day is out.`},{t:`Ignore it and take the milk`,next:`path_sandwich_leave`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You stay out of the fridge wars. You take the milk and go.`}]},{id:`cof_stolen_sandwich_2a`,char:`Markus`,title:`The Hungry Wolf`,reqStory:`path_sandwich_steal`,text:`Markus is bellowing in the corridor. 'WHO HAS BEEN AT MY PASTRAMI?! I AM HAVING A LOW-BLOOD-SUGAR CRASH! MY DEALS ARE COLLAPSING!' He looks as though he is about to cry.`,opts:[{t:`Sacrifice a stale doughnut`,rem:`donut`,rep:{Markus:5},m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You graciously hand him your stale doughnut. He eats it hurriedly. 'Thanks, Miller. You are my saviour.' Your conscience has been washed clean.`},{t:`Watch him suffer in silence`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:2,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`The pastrami in your stomach really was excellent. You say not a word and enjoy the show.`}]},{id:`cof_stolen_sandwich_2b`,char:`Markus`,title:`The War of the Names`,reqStory:`path_sandwich_prank`,text:`Markus and Egon are squaring up to each other in the kitchenette. Egon is taking a hearty bite out of the pastrami sandwich. 'It had my name on it, suit!' says Egon, mouth full. Markus gasps.`,opts:[{t:`Settle in with the popcorn`,m:10,l:10,a:-15,b:10,r:`You prop yourself against the door frame and watch the row escalate. Far better than any Netflix series.`},{t:`Step in and clear it up`,rep:{Markus:5,Egon:5},m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You end the prank. Both stare at you, dumbfounded. 'IT humour', you mutter, and disappear quickly.`}]},{id:`cof_stolen_sandwich_2c`,char:`Markus`,title:`Gone Off`,reqStory:`path_sandwich_leave`,text:`Markus was out of the office yesterday. The sinfully expensive sandwich is still lying in the fridge today. The bread has gone completely soggy and looks grey.`,opts:[{t:`Quietly dispose of the revolting thing`,m:5,l:-5,a:5,b:-5,r:`You sacrifice yourself for the hygiene of the kitchenette and throw it away. Nobody thanks you, and the smell has gone.`},{t:`Laugh at Markus by email`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:2,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You send him an email: 'Your sandwich is currently mutating.' He replies with nothing but a crying smiley.`}]},{id:`cof_grinder_1`,title:`Deafening`,text:`The expensive coffee machine is grinding the beans today with a noise reminiscent of a jet taking off. The vibrations make the mugs rattle in the cupboard. Something in the grinder is jammed, and badly.`,opts:[{t:`Deal it one decisive blow`,next:`path_grinder_hit`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`BAM. You strike the side with the flat of your hand. The shrieking stops instantly. The machine purrs again. Violence is a solution after all.`},{t:`Switch the machine off and raise a ticket with HR`,next:`path_grinder_ticket`,m:5,l:-5,a:10,b:5,r:`You pull the plug and hang up an 'OUT OF ORDER' sign. Half the department looks you over the way you would look at a man who has cancelled Christmas.`},{t:`See it through with your ears covered`,next:`path_grinder_endure`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You let it scream until your coffee is through. A slight ringing in the ears, and a coffee in your hand.`}]},{id:`cof_grinder_2a`,title:`The Mechanic`,reqStory:`path_grinder_hit`,text:`Your blow did calm the machine down, and now the side panel is completely loose and rattles maddeningly in time with the pump pressure.`,opts:[{t:`Ignore the rattle`,m:2,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Who needs silence in an office? You take your coffee and leave the machine clattering behind you.`},{t:`Patch it with duct tape`,req:`tape`,m:5,l:-5,a:-10,b:-5,r:`Two thick silver strips of tape solve the problem. It has the air of a building site, and the acoustics are saved.`}]},{id:`cof_grinder_2b`,title:`The Coffee Uprising`,reqStory:`path_grinder_ticket`,text:`The machine is still standing idle. An angry knot of staff has formed in the corridor. The mood is extremely hostile. Somebody whispers: 'IT broke the thing.'`,opts:[{t:`Surrender and make instant coffee`,m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:-10,r:`You dig out the old powder. It tastes of damp earth, and it stops the mutiny before it starts.`},{t:`Flee and lock yourself in the office`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:10,r:`You flee to your office and turn the key. Let the caffeine addicts devour each other.`}]},{id:`cof_grinder_2c`,title:`Explosion`,reqStory:`path_grinder_endure`,text:`You should not have forced the machine to keep running. The grinder burst shortly afterwards with a loud bang. Coffee grounds are stuck all the way up to the ceiling.`,opts:[{t:`Withdraw quietly from the crime scene`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:10,r:`You turn round without comment. Whoever clears that up is definitely not going to enjoy it.`},{t:`Summon Egon by priority ticket`,rep:{Egon:-5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:-5,r:`You call the caretaker. Egon sees the grounds on the ceiling and loses all faith in humanity.`}]},{id:`cof_workout_2a`,char:`Chantal`,title:`Aching Muscles`,reqStory:`path_workout_join`,text:`You drag yourself to the coffee machine. The 90-minute Pilates class on the floor is exacting its price. You can barely lift your arms for the pain to reach for the cup. Chantal stands beside you, superbly fit and fresh.`,opts:[{t:`Ask her to pass you the coffee`,rep:{Chantal:10},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Chantal laughs. 'Haha, beginner! You have potential, though.' She hands you the cup. You have gained a friend, even if your body is 80 years old today.`},{t:`Draw it yourself, through the pain`,m:5,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`You clench your teeth and raise your arm, trembling. Every muscle burns. Rarely has a coffee been so thoroughly earned, and your arms shake for an hour afterwards.`}]},{id:`cof_dance_1`,title:`Smooth Criminal`,text:`You fetch yourself a coffee. The room is empty. 'Billie Jean' is stuck in your head and you let yourself go. You pull off a perfect moonwalk, grab your crotch and execute a wild spin. When you open your eyes you are staring straight into a running camera lens. Behind it the boss is giving a live interview for the 'GlobalCorp Investor Day'.`,opts:[{t:`Run for it in a panic`,next:`path_dance_flee`,m:5,l:0,a:30,b:10,r:`Your eyes go wide, you let out a small shriek and sprint out of shot. An unspeakably embarrassing exit, now preserved for ever in the company archive and on the internet.`},{t:`Finish the dance with total composure`,next:`path_dance_finish`,m:10,l:10,a:-10,b:15,r:`In for a penny! You tip an imaginary hat, glide backwards out of shot and vanish, coolly. The investors on the stream go wild with delight.`},{t:`Cover the camera lens with the doughnut`,rem:`donut`,next:`path_dance_donut`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:20,r:`In a panic you press your sticky doughnut straight onto the cameraman's sinfully expensive lens. Picture black. Evidence (partly) destroyed, cameraman raging.`}]},{id:`cof_advent_july`,title:`Looking Forward to It`,text:`Chantal is standing in the kitchen in front of an open box of Christmas decorations. It is July.

'I thought we would start EARLY this year! Positive energy in the team! I just need somebody to put the string of lights up.'

She looks at you. Only you.`,char:`Chantal`,opts:[{t:`'Chantal. It is July.'`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,rep:{Chantal:-10},r:`'And? Joy does not keep a calendar.' She says it entirely without irony. Three weeks later the box is still standing there, half unpacked, like a memorial to good intentions.`},{t:`Climb onto the chair and hang it up.`,loot:`zip_ties`,m:25,l:-10,a:15,b:0,rep:{Chantal:10},r:`Twenty minutes balancing on an office chair. The string hangs crooked. Chantal is delighted. You keep the leftover cable ties — she is certainly not going to need them in July.`},{t:`'I will need a hammer for that first.'`,loot:`hammer`,m:10,l:10,a:0,b:0,rep:{Chantal:-5},r:`You fetch a hammer from Stores, come back, and Chantal is in a meeting. The box is still standing there. The hammer stays with you.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_razzia`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`The Raid`,text:`Ms Elster stands at the open fridge in rubber gloves, holding a list. On the table: a row of containers, like defendants in the dock. 'Use-by date inspection, Mr Miller. And THIS', she lifts a yoghurt, 'is labelled with your name. The thirteenth of July.'`,opts:[{t:`Evacuate the yoghurt on the quiet`,next:`path_razzia_schmuggel`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`A diversion ('Is that mould back there?'), a quick grab, and the yoghurt is in your jacket pocket. You have just saved food from Accounts. All you have to do now is remember that it is in your pocket.`},{t:`Help with the raid, guiltily`,loot:`chocolate`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},next:`path_razzia_helfen`,m:10,l:0,a:10,b:-5,r:`You sacrifice the yoghurt and assist with the inspection. By way of thanks she presses a confiscated but flawless bar of chocolate into your hand: 'The best-before date is a recommendation. With chocolate.' It is the kindest thing she has ever said.`},{t:`Defend the yoghurt: 'It is still alive'`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-5},next:`path_razzia_protest`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Yoghurt IS a bacterial culture, Ms Elster. It only gets better.' She stares at you as though you had insulted the tax office. The yoghurt goes in the bin regardless. You made a stand, and that will have consequences.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_razzia_2a`,title:`The Artefact`,reqStory:`path_razzia_helfen`,text:`Right at the back of the bottom shelf you find it: a misted-up container with no label. Ms Elster holds it up to the light at arm's length. 'That was already here when I started.' She started in 2019. You look at each other.`,opts:[{t:`Dispose of it unopened, double-bagged`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`Some truths belong in two bags and then in the general waste bin in the yard. You carry the container out together, with the dignity of a burial at sea. What was inside remains for ever a theory.`},{t:`Hand it to Egon - he knows about these things`,rep:{Egon:3},m:5,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`Egon looks at the container, gives it a brief shake and nods: 'I know that one. That is Krause's. He left in 2016.' He takes it down to the basement. You do not ask whether Room K3 has a shelf for such things. It has.`},{t:`Open it. Somebody has to.`,m:5,l:0,a:15,b:0,r:`The lid comes away with a hiss that is not of this world. The smell reaches corners of the kitchen no smell has ever reached. Ms Elster throws the window open. You never speak of it again. There are things between you now.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_razzia_2b`,title:`The List`,reqStory:`path_razzia_protest`,text:`There is a new notice on the fridge: 'Delinquent foodstuffs and their keepers'. One name is on it. Yours. Beside it, in brackets and in Elster's precise handwriting: '(unrepentant)'.`,opts:[{t:`Apologise and make peace`,rep:{"Frau Elster":5},m:10,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`You bring her a fresh yoghurt with today's date as a peace offering. She checks the best-before date, nods and takes your name off the list. 'Insight', she says, 'is the first step towards order.'`},{t:`Lodge a formal objection`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-3},m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`You compose an objection with a subject line, a file reference and footnotes. Ms Elster reads it twice and files it - in a folder called 'Matters M.' You could have done without learning that this folder exists. The objection is running, though.`},{t:`'Lose' the notice`,m:2,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`The notice falls tragically behind the fridge, where the cleaning staff have not reached since 2015. Ms Elster will notice its absence. Ms Elster notices everything. The only question is what version two of the list will contain.`}]},{id:`cof_elster_razzia_2c`,title:`The Fugitive`,reqStory:`path_razzia_schmuggel`,text:`A sweetish smell drifts through the office. The source: your jacket. The evacuated yoghurt could not withstand the pressure of freedom and has unfolded itself in your inside pocket. Extensively.`,opts:[{t:`Simply zip the jacket up`,m:2,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`Zip closed, problem sealed. You now smell discreetly of strawberry-vanilla with a top note of decomposition. Colleagues hold their breath as they pass, without making a thing of it. The boss has a meeting with you later today.`},{t:`'Bequeath' the jacket to Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:-5},m:5,l:10,a:0,b:0,r:`'Kevin, this one is too small for me. Do you want it?' Kevin beams and puts it on immediately. The smell reaches him after exactly four minutes. He carries on wearing it regardless, out of pride. You are officially a bad person.`},{t:`Deep-clean the jacket`,m:15,l:-5,a:10,b:0,r:`Fifteen minutes with washing-up liquid and paper towels at the sink. The jacket survives, your pride not entirely. The yoghurt won after all. Ms Elster would enjoy that punchline.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_maschine`,char:`Dr. Wichtig`,title:`The Usual`,text:`Dr Wichtig is at the coffee machine, at a loss. 'Miller. This machine has two buttons. On the board we have one with fourteen. Make me what I always drink.' You do not know what he always drinks. Nobody knows that. Probably not even he does.`,opts:[{t:`Put on a barista performance`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},next:`path_ueblich_show`,m:15,l:10,a:5,b:0,r:`You froth milk in the kettle, tap the cup expertly and serve 'a flat white, Melbourne style'. It is button 1 with foam. Dr Wichtig is delighted. Too delighted. He is going to want this again.`},{t:`Press button 1 and serve with composure`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":3},next:`path_ueblich_bluff`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:-5,r:`You press button 1 and hand the cup over with the expression of a sommelier. He sips. 'Exactly right.' It was button 1. It is always button 1. That information is your capital now.`},{t:`Ask honestly what it is he drinks`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-3},next:`path_ueblich_frage`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`'The... usual. With the crema signature.' He becomes visibly impatient - leaders do not explain, they expect. You press some button or other. He drinks it without a word and goes. That was not a pass.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_maschine_2a`,title:`Coffee Briefing 09:15`,reqStory:`path_ueblich_bluff`,text:`There is a new recurring meeting in your calendar: 'Coffee briefing with Dr. W., daily 09:15, kitchen'. Invited: you. Agenda: none. You have apparently become the official translator between the boss and button 1.`,opts:[{t:`'Calibrate' a flask`,m:15,l:-5,a:-10,b:-5,r:`Every morning you leave a prepared flask with the label 'THE USUAL - CALIBRATED'. Dr Wichtig is deeply impressed by the process optimisation. The meeting disappears from the calendar; the legend remains.`},{t:`Simply accept the meeting`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":3},m:10,l:0,a:10,b:-5,r:`Ten minutes of handing over coffee and small talk about 'visions' every morning. It is absurd, and it is also the shortest line to the boss any admin has ever had. Word has it Markus is envious of the meeting.`},{t:`Let Gabi in on it and hand it over`,rep:{Gabi:5},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`Gabi listens to the secret of button 1 and smiles mildly: 'I have been doing that with his tea for years.' From tomorrow Reception takes over the briefing. Dr Wichtig does not notice the difference. He would not, naturally.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_maschine_2b`,title:`Fourteen Buttons`,reqStory:`path_ueblich_frage`,text:`There is a pallet outside the kitchen. Dr Wichtig has had the board's machine ordered 'to remedy the competence gap': fourteen buttons, seven languages, a touch display. Ms Elster stands beside it holding an invoice like a declaration of war.`,opts:[{t:`Quietly 'simplify' the machine`,m:10,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`You configure all fourteen buttons to the same drink: button 1 of the old machine. Colleagues rave about the 'consistency at board level'. Should an engineer ever read the configuration out, you will have some explaining to do.`},{t:`Have to explain the invoice to Ms Elster`,rep:{"Frau Elster":-3},m:10,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`'FOUR THOUSAND euros, Mr Miller. For COFFEE.' You explain that all you did was ask a question. Ms Elster notes something in her little book. The causation principle: the boss may have ordered the invoice, the question came from you.`},{t:`Brief all the colleagues`,m:20,l:0,a:10,b:-5,r:`Twenty minutes of training, fourteen buttons, zero comprehension. Everybody drinks 'Café Crème' afterwards anyway, because that is the first button. The briefing is documented, though, and documented beats sensible. Always.`}]},{id:`cof_ceo_maschine_2c`,title:`The Board's Barista`,reqStory:`path_ueblich_show`,text:`An email from the board secretariat: 'Dr Wichtig would like your coffee specialities (Melbourne style) for eight people for this afternoon's board meeting.' There is no Melbourne style. There is button 1 and a kettle.`,opts:[{t:`Let Chantal turn it into an 'event'`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:10,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`Chantal takes it on with burning enthusiasm: she calls it a 'Coffee Experience', prints menu cards and sets out a scented candle. The coffee is still button 1. The verdict on the meeting: 'best catering in years'. Marketing works.`},{t:`'I am an admin, not a barista.'`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":-5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`Your polite refusal is 'noted' by the secretariat. The next time he passes, Dr Wichtig mentions casually that 'a willingness to serve is a leadership criterion'. You are not a leader. Precisely, says his look.`},{t:`Go through with the catering`,rep:{"Dr. Wichtig":5},m:25,l:10,a:10,b:0,r:`Eight cups of button 1, eight caps of kettle foam, an improvised tray. The board are enchanted; one of them asks about the 'provenance of the beans'. You say 'single origin, machine three'. Nobody laughs. Everybody nods.`}]},{id:`cof_entkalken`,title:`DESCALE`,text:`The coffee machine shows in red capitals: 'DESCALE'. It refuses to dispense anything further. In twenty minutes the breakfast break starts, and then there will be a crowd standing here with empty cups and dwindling patience. You know this crowd. You fear this crowd.`,opts:[{t:`Descale it properly`,next:`path_kalk_pflege`,m:20,l:-5,a:10,b:-5,r:`Mix the descaler, start the programme, wait out three rinse cycles - while the first cups clink outside. The machine runs afterwards as it did on its first day. Possibly a shade too well.`},{t:`Hold the button until the message goes away`,next:`path_kalk_ignor`,m:2,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`Eight seconds on the button, message gone, machine running. A trick a service engineer once showed you - with the words 'but only in an emergency'. It is an emergency every time now. The limescale is accruing interest.`},{t:`Improvise with kitchen vinegar`,next:`path_kalk_essig`,m:10,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`No descaler in the building, but there is vinegar essence in the cleaning cupboard. The machine gurgles, offended, and runs again. The first coffee afterwards has a top note that could politely be described as 'vinaigrette'.`}]},{id:`cof_entkalken_2a`,title:`Maintained Too Well`,reqStory:`path_kalk_pflege`,text:`The descaled machine runs with the pressure of its youth - and doses noticeably stronger than it has in the last three years. Half the company is over-caffeinated. Chantal has scheduled four meetings since 11:00, Kevin speaks exclusively in exclamation marks.`,opts:[{t:`Let it run - productivity!`,m:2,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`The company vibrates. Ticket numbers fall, the volume rises, somebody has just polished the stairwell, voluntarily. This cannot possibly end healthily; until it does, it is impressive to watch.`},{t:`Put up a warning sign`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,r:`'CAUTION: STRONG. Observe the dose.' The sign is photographed, shared in three chat groups and completely ignored. It is up there, though. If it comes to it, you warned them, and 'warned them if it comes to it' is half the battle in this company.`},{t:`Gently turn the dose down`,m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You step the machine back down to the accustomed level of 'brown water with intentions'. The company settles over the course of the afternoon. Nobody thanks you. Nobody even knows what you prevented.`}]},{id:`cof_entkalken_2b`,title:`The Fall of the Machine`,reqStory:`path_kalk_ignor`,text:`It has happened: the machine fell silent mid-extraction. Finally, with one last rattle that sounded of limescale and reproach. A queue forms. Kevin has opened his backpack and whispers: 'I have instant here. Fifty cents a cup.'`,opts:[{t:`Hang a note up: 'OUT OF ORDER - engineer informed'`,m:2,l:10,a:5,b:5,r:`The note is patient, the queue is not. No engineer has been informed - the note IS the measure. Colleagues make the grumbling pilgrimage to the petrol station opposite. Somebody will ask when the engineer is coming. Daily.`},{t:`Emergency surgery on the machine`,m:20,l:-5,a:15,b:-5,r:`You dismantle the brew head in front of an audience. The lump of limescale you operate out is the size of a walnut and is met by the queue with an awed murmur. The machine lives again. You are a hero for today. For today.`},{t:`Tolerate Kevin's instant empire`,rep:{Kevin:3},m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`Kevin does the business of his life. He has change, a kettle and, from the second hour, a loyalty scheme ('Tenth cup free'). The coffee is dreadful. The entrepreneurial spirit is not.`}]},{id:`cof_entkalken_2c`,title:`Vinaigrette`,reqStory:`path_kalk_essig`,text:`The vinegar is more persistent than planned. The fifth coffee of the day still tastes of salad dressing, and the complaints are getting more creative. Chantal, on the other hand, has posted a story: 'Our office does DETOX coffee now! So clean!' Forty likes.`,opts:[{t:`Rinse thoroughly until it is over`,m:15,l:-5,a:-10,b:0,r:`Six rinse cycles, two jugs of fresh water, one sacrificial espresso as a test. The vinegar capitulates. The coffee tastes of coffee again, which is to say of almost nothing, and everybody is content. Normality is underrated.`},{t:`Back Chantal's detox framing`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:5,l:10,a:0,b:0,r:`When asked, you confirm 'yes, apple cider vinegar infusion, very much in vogue'. Chantal tags you as 'our wellness admin'. Three colleagues now drink it with CONVICTION. The vinegar wears off by itself; the legend does not.`},{t:`Declare it a premium innovation`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`'Cold-brew cleansing cycle, running until Friday.' The complaints fall silent - you cannot complain about innovation in this company, that would be backward. Should Dr Wichtig get wind of it, he will want it in the portfolio.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_termin`,char:`Markus`,title:`11:00`,text:`Markus is standing at the coffee machine, uncharacteristically still, stirring an empty cup and has been for minutes. 'Miller. Today, 11:00. TechniPlast, board presentation. If that comes off, the quarter is saved.' No 'time is money', no alpha posturing. For the first time he looks like somebody who does not believe in himself.`,opts:[{t:`Hear the pitch and help sharpen it`,rep:{Markus:10},next:`path_lampen_coach`,m:20,l:10,a:5,b:0,r:`He pitches the presentation at you and you repair the technical slides: 'infinitely scalable' becomes 'scalable', 'military-grade encryption' becomes 'current best practice'. Markus listens. Genuinely listens. Twenty minutes of your working time, well invested. Probably.`},{t:`'Chin up'`,rep:{Markus:-3},next:`path_lampen_floskel`,m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`The platitude hits the floor like a wet cloth. Markus nods mechanically: 'Yes. Right. Chin up.' He takes his coffee and goes. You could have invested two minutes. You invested two words.`},{t:`Brew a lucky coffee: button 2`,rep:{Markus:5},next:`path_lampen_kaffee`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Button 2, double crema. Only people who win drink that one round here.' Complete nonsense, and Markus clutches the cup like a talisman. 'Button 2', he repeats, seriously. Ritual beats truth, and always has.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_termin_2a`,title:`The Technical Man`,reqStory:`path_lampen_coach`,text:`Bellowing from the corridor, and this time the good kind: 'A CLOSING! TechniPlast have signed!' Markus sweeps into the kitchen, points at you and announces to the assembled breakfast gathering: 'MY technical man! Without him that would have come to nothing!' Everybody looks at you.`,opts:[{t:`Cheekily demand a commission`,rep:{Markus:5},m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`'Two per cent, Markus.' He stares at you - then breaks into booming laughter: 'NEGOTIATING! I have trained you well!' There are no two per cent. There is a coffee on the house and his respect. The latter is rarer.`},{t:`Accept the glory`,rep:{Markus:5},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:-5,r:`You accept the applause with a nod. 'Technical man' is your title in Sales from here on - which means: Sales have your extension from here on. Glory in this company is only another word for availability.`},{t:`Make clear that it was a one-off`,rep:{Markus:-3},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'A one-off, Markus. I have a job of my own.' He waves it away generously: 'Sure, sure. A one-off.' You both know he will be standing at the machine again in two weeks. The line is drawn, though, for the record.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_termin_2b`,title:`Not His Day`,reqStory:`path_lampen_floskel`,text:`Markus comes back in the afternoon, tie loosened, shoulders low. 'Adjourned. They want to sleep on it.' He sits down on the worktop, which he never does. 'I floundered on the technical part, Miller. Really floundered.'`,opts:[{t:`Offer to analyse the feedback`,rep:{Markus:5},m:15,l:-5,a:5,b:0,r:`You go through the customer feedback together. The objections are almost all technical - and almost all solvable. Markus takes notes, real ones, on paper. 'Adjourned is not lost', he says as he leaves. It almost sounds like him again.`},{t:`Stand him a coffee and listen`,rep:{Markus:10},m:15,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You press a coffee into his hand and listen. For a quarter of an hour Markus is not a salesman but a person with self-doubt and a daughter reading business studies. Then he stands up: 'Next time you do the technical slides.' It does not sound like an order. It sounds like a request.`},{t:`'It will come off next time'`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:2,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`The second platitude of the day. Markus looks at you briefly, and in that look lies the exact bookkeeping of who was there when it counted and who handed out calendar mottoes. He nods and goes. The account is in the red.`}]},{id:`cof_markus_termin_2c`,title:`The Lucky Button`,reqStory:`path_lampen_kaffee`,text:`The deal is through, and Markus has told the story of the lucky coffee to the whole of Sales. Since then the entire department presses nothing but button 2. A small procession forms before every customer meeting. Button 2 is already beginning to stick with fatigue.`,opts:[{t:`Tell Chantal about 'button 2'`,rep:{Chantal:3},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`Chantal scents content and produces an Insta post: 'The success espresso - only here.' Stickers follow, a hashtag, and the idea of making button 2 'an experience' at company events. You have turned an office joke into a brand. May it never belong to you.`},{t:`End the myth: it is only coffee`,rep:{Markus:-3},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'That was a joke, everybody. Button 2 is button 1 with more water.' Awkward silence across Sales. Markus shakes his head in disappointment: 'Some things you do not talk to death, Miller.' The procession carries on regardless. Only without you.`},{t:`Tend the myth and service the button`,m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You quietly replace the spring under button 2 and polish it. Faith needs working infrastructure. Sales have their best figures this quarter in years. Correlation, causation - who cares about that at button 2.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeekasse`,title:`The Honesty Box`,text:`The coffee kitty is empty. The tally sheet beside it counts 34 coffees since Monday; the piggy bank contains one button, one paper clip and one receipt from 2023. Gabi is propped against the door frame: 'I know who it was. But I will say only this much: it is more complicated than you think.'`,opts:[{t:`'Sponsor' the box with the 'Black Card'`,req:`black_card`,next:`path_kasse_amex`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:5,r:`You hold Prince Abubakar's card ceremonially against the piggy bank. There is no terminal. There will never be a terminal. You put cash in instead, with the gesture of a man whose limit is a pure illusion. Two colleagues saw it. There will be rumours.`},{t:`Question Gabi - she knows everything`,rep:{Gabi:3},next:`path_kasse_spur`,m:10,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Gabi talks in concentric circles: first about the weather, then about the canteen, then about 'somebody who always puts it back. Mostly.' By the time she finishes you know: this is not theft. It is something sadder. And you still do not know who.`},{t:`Install a dummy camera`,next:`path_kasse_kamera`,m:10,l:5,a:0,b:5,r:`An old webcam with no cable, a red LED sticker, directly above the box. Deterrence by theatre. There are coins in the pig again the same day. And somebody asks about the data protection impact assessment the same day.`},{t:`Top it up yourself, without a word`,next:`path_kasse_engel`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You put your own money in. Peace is cheaper than truth, and honestly you would rather not know which colleague is failing at the coffee kitty. The pig jingles again. For now.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeekasse_2a`,title:`End of the Month`,reqStory:`path_kasse_spur`,text:`The trail leads to a piece of knowledge you would rather not have: it is Kevin. Apprentice pay, end of the month, and the coffee kitty as a quiet bridging loan. He always puts it back on the first. Mostly. Gabi knew all along and said nothing. Now you know as well.`,opts:[{t:`Report it correctly to Ms Elster`,rep:{Kevin:-10,"Frau Elster":3},m:5,l:0,a:5,b:-5,r:`Ms Elster receives the report and handles the case 'by the rules': a reprimand, a file note, a repayment plan over four weeks. All correct. Kevin no longer says hello to you in the corridor. That is correct as well.`},{t:`Discreetly set up an 'IT fund'`,rep:{Kevin:10},m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You set out a second tin: 'IT emergency box - help yourselves, pay it back, no questions.' Kevin understands the message without a word ever being said. From the next month the coffee kitty balances again. The emergency box fluctuates. That is fine. That is what it is for.`},{t:`Raise it gently with Kevin`,rep:{Kevin:5},m:10,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Kevin goes red to the brim of his cap. 'I ALWAYS put it back!' Nearly true. You talk briefly about apprentice pay and canteen prices. You end up lending him a twenty until the first - officially, between men. He pays it back on time. He is proud of that now.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeekasse_2b`,title:`The Impact Assessment`,reqStory:`path_kasse_kamera`,text:`Chantal has discovered the dummy camera and called a meeting: 'Awareness session: surveillance in the workplace'. She has slides. She has the Works Council in CC. The camera has no cable, and nobody but you knows that.`,opts:[{t:`Make Chantal the 'data protection ambassador'`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`'Chantal, this subject needs a face. Yours.' She accepts the mission, designs a badge and forgets the camera entirely in the process. The dummy stays up, now more or less under the protection of the ambassador herself. Distraction does not come more elegant than that.`},{t:`Expose the camera as a dummy`,m:10,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You hold the cableless camera up like an exhibit. Relief, laughter, a single accusation ('Psychological surveillance is ALSO surveillance!'). The meeting ends after ten minutes. The box has stayed full ever since. Theatre works, even when exposed.`},{t:`Sit the meeting out in full`,m:15,l:10,a:10,b:0,r:`Forty-five slides on the General Data Protection Regulation, delivered by somebody who cannot open a PDF. You say nothing. The dummy stays up and so does its secret. Silence, now and then, is the most efficient lie.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeekasse_2c`,title:`The Suspicion`,reqStory:`path_kasse_engel`,text:`Somebody watched you putting money in - from behind, partly, in passing. The result is already going round the office grapevine: 'Miller is topping the box up. Why would that be? Because HE empties it and has a guilty conscience.' The prime suspect in your own good deed is you.`,opts:[{t:`Set the record straight publicly`,m:10,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You explain what actually happened to the breakfast gathering. Half of them believe you. The other half think that is exactly what the box thief would say. Truth scales badly against a good story. Half is still half.`},{t:`Simply carry the reputation`,m:2,l:10,a:5,b:5,r:`Let them talk. You know what is true, and explanations only ennoble the rumour. The office grapevine loses interest after two days - a residue remains, though. A residue always remains. The boss likes hearing residues of that kind.`},{t:`Ask Gabi for a counter-rumour`,rep:{Gabi:3},m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Gabi listens to the problem and nods with professional authority: 'Nobody will be talking about it by Thursday.' On Wednesday the whole company is discussing the supposed engagement in Accounts. Your story is dead. Never ask what she put into circulation for it.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeekasse_2d`,title:`The Prince from IT`,reqStory:`path_kasse_amex`,text:`The rumour gathered pace overnight: Miller owns a 'Black Card'. Miller is secretly wealthy. Miller does the admin job 'purely out of passion'. Markus heads you off at the machine, eyes shining: 'We need to talk about your portfolio.'`,opts:[{t:`Deny it soberly`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`'The card belongs to a Nigerian prince, Markus.' He laughs booming and punches your arm matily: 'DISCRETION! Understood. Old money does not talk.' The denial has just confirmed the rumour. That is how rumours work.`},{t:`Let Markus run into it`,rep:{Markus:-5},m:10,l:5,a:-10,b:0,r:`You let him present 'exclusive investment opportunities' at you for a quarter of an hour, nod knowingly and finish with: 'My family office handles that.' Markus withdraws reverently to google what a family office is. It was glorious.`},{t:`Actively tend the legend`,m:5,l:10,a:-5,b:10,r:`You deny nothing, smile enigmatically and pay for your canteen lunch in coins, pointedly casually. The legend grows. People hold doors open for you. At some point Dr Wichtig will ask why a wealthy man does not renegotiate his salary band - or Ms Elster where the wealth comes from.`}]},{id:`cof_falle_bio`,char:`Chantal`,title:`The Organic Beans`,text:`Chantal places a bag on the machine, ceremonially: 'Organic! Fairtrade! Single origin! We are going to fill it with these, yes? For the values.' The bag glistens oily. The machine is a 2014 model and has only ever accepted ordinary beans grudgingly.`,opts:[{t:`'The machine will not take that.'`,rep:{Chantal:-5},m:5,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`Technically correct, socially a minefield. Chantal privately files you under 'refuses progress', and the discussion about the machine tolerance of ideals costs you a quarter of an hour of joy in five minutes.`},{t:`Secretly fill the organic bag with the old beans`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`In organic clothing the supermarket coffee tastes 'soooo much rounder' (Chantal). The deception works perfectly - and that is exactly the problem: you have to repeat it every week now, for ever, and one day somebody will be standing next to you while you decant.`},{t:`Gladly - values have to be lived`,rep:{Chantal:5},m:10,l:0,a:30,b:10,r:`The oily beans gum the grinder up completely after four extractions. The machine stops, the queue grows, and Chantal tells everybody that YOU 'made the switch'. Values have to be lived. So do repairs.`}]},{id:`cof_falle_letzte_tasse`,title:`The Last Cup`,text:`The pot is nearly empty - enough left for about three-quarters of a cup. The house law is unambiguous: take the last cup and you make a fresh pot. Footsteps are approaching in the corridor. You have roughly four seconds to decide.`,opts:[{t:`Go without and return empty-handed`,m:2,l:5,a:15,b:0,r:`You leave with an empty cup and a full principle. The afternoon without caffeine drags like an alignment meeting, and behind you you hear somebody else take the last cup perfectly calmly and NOT make a fresh pot. There is no justice. There is only coffee, and you do not have any.`},{t:`Take only half a mouthful, just in case`,m:2,l:5,a:10,b:25,r:`The oldest trick in the office world - and at that exact moment Ms Elster steps into the kitchen and sees you, pot in hand, leaving a strategic residue. Her look re-catalogues you. The remaining centimetre of coffee stands there for another three days as a memorial.`},{t:`Take the last cup and put a fresh pot on`,m:15,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`Compliant and honourable: you take the last cup and make a fresh pot. It takes a while, the machine gurgles, three people waiting watch you like a building-site crane, and one asks whether it will be 'much longer'. Honour eats time.`}]},{id:`cof_falle_spende`,title:`The Charity Run`,text:`Bernd from Sales is standing at the machine with a list: 'I am running in the company run! For a good cause! Will you put your name down? Two euros a kilometre, it is only ten kilometres.' Twenty euros. The list is well filled. Everybody is watching.`,opts:[{t:`Sign up generously - for a good cause`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:20,r:`Twenty euros, a good feeling - and an entry in an invisible register: you now count as 'always donates'. Over the next few weeks the cake sale, the raffle, the shirt sponsorship and Bernd's second run will all find you. Generosity in this building is a subscription.`},{t:`Give a symbolic five euros`,m:2,l:0,a:5,b:5,r:`The classic compromise. Bernd says 'five euros helps too!' in a tone that means the opposite, and the smallest figure on the list now stands beside your name for all to see. You have paid AND you count as tight-fisted. The worst of both worlds, at a special price.`},{t:`Decline politely`,m:2,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`'Bad month, sorry.' Bernd nods understandingly and passes it on understandingly. Photographs are taken at the company run, there is a thank-you all-staff email with every donor's name on it, and yours is missing. Nobody says anything. Everybody knows.`}]},{id:`cof_schacht_1`,char:`Frau Elster`,title:`Position Seven`,text:`Ms Elster heads you off at the coffee machine, folder under her arm, working through her list. 'Mr Miller, the entries are almost all allocated. Only position seven is still open. Position seven. Always that seven.'`,opts:[{t:`Help her with the allocation`,rep:{"Frau Elster":3},next:`path_schacht_1`,m:15,l:-5,a:5,b:-5,r:`You go through the list together; position seven is a wrongly coded printer toner. As she takes her leave she says something else - and for a fraction of a second you are certain she said 'The shaft does not forget'. You watched television too long last night. Four episodes. It is catching up with you.`},{t:`Refer her to Accounts`,next:`path_schacht_1`,m:5,l:10,a:0,b:5,r:`'That is more one for Accounts, Ms Elster.' She IS Accounts. As she leaves she mutters something that sounds like 'What lies below does not stay below'. Must be you. Four episodes of SCHACHT 7 in one evening was possibly too much.`},{t:`Put her off pleasantly`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`You promise to see to it later, and you even mean it. Ms Elster nods and moves on, the folder held against her chest like a shield. A perfectly normal matter on a perfectly normal morning.`}]},{id:`cof_kaffeetrick_schlange`,reqStory:`path_chef_kaffeetrick`,title:`Queue at the Machine`,text:`There are seven people standing in front of the machine. Each one presses espresso, holds the cup sensor shut and waits for the premium roast. The machine hands it over, every time, with a noise it never used to make.

All you wanted was a coffee.`,opts:[{t:`Tape the sensor over with duct tape`,rem:`tape`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:5,r:`You tape the cup sensor over. The trick stops working, the machine survives, and nobody knows why it is suddenly over. Your duct tape is gone, and it died for something.`},{t:`Join the queue and join in`,m:20,l:10,a:-10,b:10,r:`Twenty minutes in the queue, and in exchange the best coffee this building has to offer. When your turn comes you hold the sensor shut like everybody else, and the machine makes its noise for you too. The lost time is the price, and today you pay it gladly.`},{t:`Wait until the queue has gone`,m:25,l:15,a:-5,b:0,r:`You wait in the corridor until the kitchenette is empty and then pull an ordinary coffee in peace. It tastes the way it always tastes. Nobody spoke to you, and today that was worth more.`},{t:`Lock the machine before it breaks`,m:15,l:-10,a:15,b:-10,rep:{Chantal:-5,Markus:-5},r:`You put the machine into service mode and hang a note on it. Seven people watch you do it. Four of them will be telling people before the day is out that IT took their coffee away.`}]},{id:`cof_gabi_vorrat`,reqStory:`path_gabi_kollaps`,char:`Gabi`,title:`The Drawer`,text:`Gabi is at the sink, putting a bag away in the low cupboard. Glucose tablets, two bars, a packet of biscuits.

'The paramedic said I should always have something in. You know where it is.'`,opts:[{t:`Add something of your own`,rem:`sandwich`,m:5,l:5,a:-15,b:0,rep:{Gabi:10},r:`You put your filled roll in with it, without saying anything. She says nothing either. From today the low cupboard in the kitchenette is a shared concern, and that is worth more than the roll.`},{t:`Help yourself, she offered`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,loot:`chocolate`,rep:{Gabi:5},r:`You take a bar. She nods, satisfied, as though she had been waiting for the offer to be accepted. A supply nobody touches is not a supply, it is a reproach.`},{t:`Decline and fetch coffee instead`,m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`You stay with coffee and decline politely. You stand in the kitchenette for ten minutes together, talking about nothing in particular. They are the most relaxed ten minutes of the day.`}]},{id:`cof_freischalt_schlange`,reqStory:`path_chantal_offen`,title:`No Quiet Coffee`,text:`You are not at the machine yet and somebody is already standing next to you. 'Ah, good that I have caught you — about the blocked pages.'

Behind him somebody else is waiting. Not for the machine.`,opts:[{t:`Suggest that Chantal collects the requests`,m:15,l:0,a:-5,b:0,rep:{Chantal:-5},r:`You explain that all requests go through Chantal with immediate effect, because she raised the subject. The group finds that plausible. Chantal finds it less plausible, and does collect them.`},{t:`Put them off pleasantly and fetch coffee`,m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:5,r:`You say 'send me an email' twice and do actually reach your coffee. You have to drink it with your back to the two of them, and voices, unfortunately, come from behind as well. Somebody else was responsible for a quiet coffee today.`},{t:`Settle the matter standing up`,m:20,l:-10,a:10,b:-5,rep:{Markus:5},r:`You explain to the group in the kitchenette how the sign-off works and why it exists. Two of them understand, one does not, and your coffee is cold. From tomorrow they stop asking at the machine, which is something.`},{t:`Leave again without coffee`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`You turn round. The kitchenette is the only place in the building where you normally come down, and today it is a waiting room. You go back with more rage than you arrived with.`}]},{id:`cof_praktikant_verlegen`,reqStory:`path_puschel`,title:`The Intern at the Machine`,text:`The intern is at the machine pressing buttons in an order that leads nowhere. When he sees you he goes red.

'About the password... that was so embarrassing.'`,opts:[{t:`Ask him about the hamster`,m:10,l:0,a:-15,b:5,r:`The hamster is called Puschel, is six years old and therefore ancient for a hamster. The intern shows you fourteen photographs. You laugh for the first time today and look at all fourteen.`},{t:`Show him how the machine works`,m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`You show him the order — cup first, then strength, then type — and you both have one. Afterwards he talks for ten minutes about his degree. It is astonishingly restful to listen to somebody who wants nothing from you.`},{t:`Say that it happens to everybody`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You wave it off and tell him that one password covers every account here and that nobody has changed anything about it since 2019. He is honestly relieved and mildly appalled, both of which are appropriate.`},{t:`Avoid the subject and fetch coffee`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`You say nothing about it, fetch your coffee and go. He stays standing at the machine. It is not an unfriendly encounter, only one he will remember for longer than you will.`}]},{id:`cof_deka_1`,title:`Project Clear Head`,text:`There is a laminated notice on the coffee machine: 'PROJECT CLEAR HEAD — decaffeinated this week as a trial. Your HR department.' Underneath it, by hand, three comments already. One of them is a single word, and it is not quotable.`,opts:[{t:`Put up with it. It is only a week.`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,next:`cof_deka_brav`,r:`You drink the brown water. It tastes like coffee that has been forbidden to hold an opinion.`},{t:`Stash real coffee in the server room`,m:15,l:0,a:-5,b:5,next:`cof_deka_geheim`,r:`A French press behind the spare parts boxes, beans in a tin labelled 'M4 SCREWS'. The server room now has a trade secret.`},{t:`Complain to the Works Council`,m:25,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`The Works Council takes it 'very seriously'. It becomes agenda item 14 of the next meeting. The meeting is next month. The pilot runs this week.`}]},{id:`cof_deka_2`,reqStory:`cof_deka_brav`,reqStoryAge:1,title:`The Skull Speaks Up`,text:`There has been a dull pressure behind your forehead since you got up, and it has a name: withdrawal. A small group is already standing at the machine, staring at the notice like a death announcement.`,opts:[{t:`Hold out and drink water`,m:10,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`You drink water. It helps with thirst. With everything else it does not help.`},{t:`Knead the stress ball until it passes`,req:`stressball`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`Knead, breathe, knead. The pressure stays, and it has competition now. The ball looks as though it is having a difficult week.`},{t:`Ask Kevin about his secret supply`,m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:5,rep:{Kevin:5},r:`Kevin pulls a flask out of his backpack without a word and pours you a cup. He asks no questions. He only notes something in a little book.`}]},{id:`cof_deka_3`,reqStory:`cof_deka_brav`,reqStoryAge:2,title:`The Notice Has Gone`,text:`All that is stuck to the machine is a remnant of laminating film. Beside it a new note, smaller, no logo: 'Pilot terminated early. Evaluation to follow.' The machine smells of coffee again. Of real coffee.`,opts:[{t:`Make a ceremony of the first proper coffee`,m:15,l:0,a:-15,b:0,r:`You take the cup in both hands and drink standing up, slowly, with your eyes shut. Somewhere behind your forehead the pressure packs its things. You have survived things this week. This counts among them.`},{t:`Ask why the pilot ended so quickly`,m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`The answer is in no email, but the kitchenette knows: the error rate in Accounts. Ms Sonntag is said to have sent three transfers to Liechtenstein. By accident. All three.`},{t:`Carry the news from door to door`,m:15,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`You work the corridor like a town crier: 'The machine can do it again.' Doors open, mugs are seized, somebody applauds quietly. For ten minutes you are the most popular person on the whole floor, and it was not even your doing.`}]},{id:`cof_deka_4`,reqStory:`cof_deka_geheim`,reqStoryAge:1,title:`The Evaluation Praises You`,text:`The interim report on the pilot project is in your pigeonhole, and one sentence is highlighted in yellow: 'The IT department in particular demonstrates that constant performance is possible without caffeine as well.' You read it twice. In the server room stands a tin labelled 'M4 SCREWS'.`,opts:[{t:`Pocket the praise without comment`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:-5,r:`You print the sentence out and hang it in the server room. Above the tin.`},{t:`Get rid of the French press as a precaution`,m:10,l:5,a:5,b:-5,r:`Whoever gets praised gets watched. The tin goes into your briefcase, the server room smells of server room again. A house move, only sadder.`},{t:`Let Kevin in on it and share the tin`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:5,rep:{Kevin:5},r:`Kevin tries it, nods, says nothing. Then he gets his little book out and notes something. The conspiracy now has two members and a file, and you very much hope that neither ever becomes relevant.`}]},{id:`cof_automat_1`,title:`The Trial Machine`,text:`Standing next to the old machine there is suddenly a second one: chrome, a display, an illuminated grinder. A Mr Kowalski is handing out business cards. 'On trial. Until the end of the week. No obligation whatsoever.' The machine hums like a promise.`,opts:[{t:`Try it, with no obligation`,m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:0,next:`cof_automat_genuss`,r:`A flat white at the touch of a button, and the crema keeps what the display promises. The old machine hums beside it like a relative being disinherited.`},{t:`Ask Kowalski where the catch is`,m:10,l:0,a:0,b:0,next:`cof_automat_genuss`,r:`'No catch. Only an offer.' He smiles like a brochure. You try it anyway. The coffee is the best thing this kitchenette has ever produced, and that is exactly what makes you suspicious.`},{t:`Do not touch it`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`Free is never free. You stay with the old machine. It does not deserve it, and neither do you.`}]},{id:`cof_automat_2`,reqStory:`cof_automat_genuss`,reqStoryAge:2,title:`Kowalski Collects`,text:`The chrome machine is tilted onto a sack truck, the display dark. Mr Kowalski is winding up the power cable, carefully, the way you peel off a plaster. 'Well?' he asks. 'Spoken to Purchasing yet?'`,opts:[{t:`Pass the offer on honestly`,m:15,l:-5,a:5,b:5,r:`You write Purchasing a factual recommendation. The answer comes back as a form: 'Requirement notification category C, processing next quarter.' Kowalski nods, as though he had read it over your shoulder. 'Until next quarter, then.'`},{t:`'Just take it away quickly.'`,m:5,l:0,a:10,b:0,r:`He understands. On the way out the sack truck squeaks once, as if in farewell. The old machine grinds pointedly loudly. Its coffee tastes of a dressing-down today.`},{t:`Take a farewell photograph`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`Kowalski takes up position beside the sack truck without being asked and poses as though for the brochure. He has evidently done this often. The photograph ends up in the team chat with the caption 'She was too good for us.' Three mourning emojis, one of them from Kevin.`}]},{id:`cof_tasse_1`,title:`The Mug Has Gone`,text:`Your mug is not at your desk. Not in the dishwasher, not in the cupboard, not behind the coffee tin. The one with the crack in the handle and the faded print. There are forty mugs in this kitchenette, and it is the one that is missing.`,opts:[{t:`Search systematically, floor by floor`,m:20,l:-5,a:5,b:0,next:`cof_tasse_spur`,r:`Three kitchenettes, two meeting rooms, one orphaned pedestal unit. Nothing. On the third floor, though, an intern says she saw 'one like that with a crack' in quality assurance yesterday. The trail is alive.`},{t:`Take some other one`,m:5,l:5,a:5,b:0,next:`cof_tasse_egal`,r:`You take a white one with the company logo. The handle sits wrong in the hand, the rim is too thick. The coffee tastes like a hotel nobody stays in voluntarily.`},{t:`Drink from a paper cup on principle`,m:5,l:0,a:5,b:0,r:`The paper cup goes soggy, the coffee tastes of lid. It is a statement, though, and statements rarely taste good.`}]},{id:`cof_tasse_2`,reqStory:`cof_tasse_spur`,reqStoryAge:1,title:`The Mug in Quality Assurance`,text:`There it is. On the desk of a Mr Petzold from quality assurance, filled with milk foam, a biscuit beside it. The crack in the handle is unmistakable. Mr Petzold is on the phone, gesturing as though he were conducting an orchestra.`,opts:[{t:`Take it off the desk without a word, mid-conversation`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:5,r:`Petzold briefly loses his thread and conducts thin air. You are already at the door. Some messages need no sound.`},{t:`Wait until he hangs up and demand it back`,m:15,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`'Oh. It was in the dishwasher, I thought—' You take the mug, tip the milk foam into the sink and rinse it twice. On the way back you carry it like a trophy.`},{t:`Stand there and watch him drink from it`,m:10,l:5,a:10,b:0,r:`Petzold drinks, conducts, drinks again. Milk foam. Out of your mug. You leave again without having said anything, and take the picture with you. It will visit you in quiet moments.`}]},{id:`cof_tasse_3`,reqStory:`cof_tasse_egal`,reqStoryAge:2,title:`It Is Back`,text:`Your mug is at your desk. Washed, dry, the crack in the handle as ever. Hanging from the handle is the tag of a teabag you never bought: rooibos vanilla. No note, no explanation. The kitchenette says nothing.`,opts:[{t:`Do not question it. Pour coffee.`,m:5,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`The handle sits in your hand like a handshake. Where it has been you will never learn, and perhaps that is all right.`},{t:`Keep the rooibos tag. As an exhibit.`,m:5,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You clip the tag to your monitor, with the other unsolved cases. Somebody in this building drinks rooibos vanilla out of other people's mugs. You will stay alert.`},{t:`Buy rooibos vanilla and stand it beside the mug`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`A whole packet, clearly visible beside the mug. If the unknown party comes back, they should be properly supplied. Trap or gift for the guest — that they may decide for themselves.`}]},{id:`cof_sonntag_1`,title:`Error Code E-52`,text:`Ms Sonntag from Accounts has stopped at the coffee machine and is reading the display like a will. 'E-52', she says as you join her. 'I have already switched it off and on again twice. That always helps with your lot otherwise.'`,opts:[{t:`'E-52. You will have to raise a ticket for that.'`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,r:`She looks at you, then at the display, then back at you. 'A ticket. For the coffee machine.' You nod seriously. The boundary of responsibility has to run somewhere, and today it runs here.`},{t:`Look at the fault and fix it`,m:10,l:-5,a:-5,b:0,next:`cof_sonntag_dank`,r:`E-52 is the grounds container. You empty it and the machine wakes up. Ms Sonntag looks as though you had pulled a child out of a well. 'You can just do that?'`},{t:`Speak sternly to the machine`,m:5,l:5,a:-5,b:0,next:`cof_sonntag_dank`,r:`You plant yourself in front of the machine and say with emphasis: 'E-52. We have discussed this.' Then you press the reset combination without drawing attention. The machine wakes up. Ms Sonntag regards you as a horse whisperer. You do not correct her.`}]},{id:`cof_sonntag_2`,reqStory:`cof_sonntag_dank`,reqStoryAge:1,title:`A Plate in the Pigeonhole`,text:`There is a small plate with cling film over it in your pigeonhole. Underneath: a slice of marble cake and a doughnut, along with a Post-it in precise bookkeeper's handwriting: 'For the gentleman from IT. The machine and I are grateful. — R. Sonntag'`,opts:[{t:`Write back in the finest bookkeeping manner`,m:10,l:0,a:-5,b:0,r:`You put a Post-it in her pigeonhole: 'Receipt confirmed. The cake has been duly posted to the books and found to be very good. With thanks, IT.' It stands a good chance of being laminated. You now have a correspondence.`},{t:`Cake now, doughnut for later`,m:10,l:0,a:-10,b:0,loot:`donut`,r:`The marble cake is home-made, with proper beating time. You eat it standing at the window and for four minutes you are at peace with everything. The doughnut goes into the drawer. An investment.`},{t:`Go and thank her in person`,m:15,l:0,a:-10,b:-5,r:`Ms Sonntag waves it away, visibly pleased all the same. 'My husband always says IT lives on biscuits.' Her husband is right. On the way back two people from Accounts say hello to you who have never said hello to you before.`}]},{id:`cof_empfang_1`,char:`Gabi`,title:`The Good Machine`,text:`It is an open secret: the best coffee machine in the building is at Reception. A proper espresso machine, well kept, Gabi's territory. As you walk past she heads you off. 'You are IT, are you not. My label printer only prints lines now. Help me out and I will show you how to make a cappuccino on that machine that deserves the name.'`,opts:[{t:`'That is what the ticket system is for.'`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,rep:{Gabi:-5},r:`Gabi raises an eyebrow and turns away. 'Then carry on drinking that stuff upstairs.' She says 'that stuff upstairs' the way other people say 'tap water'.`},{t:`Take the deal`,m:30,l:-10,a:5,b:-5,rep:{Gabi:5},next:`cof_empfang_zugang`,r:`The printer has a crumpled label jam and firmware from the day before yesterday. Twenty minutes later it is printing letters again. Gabi nods her approval. 'Tomorrow morning. First lesson.'`},{t:`Send Kevin round`,m:5,l:5,a:0,b:0,rep:{Gabi:-5},r:`Kevin comes back after twenty minutes with printer soot on his fingers and no cappuccino. 'She said she asked YOU.' The deal is off the table, and the label printer now prints lines with a sooty edge.`}]},{id:`cof_empfang_2`,reqStory:`cof_empfang_zugang`,reqStoryAge:1,title:`First Lesson on the Espresso Machine`,text:`Gabi stands next to you at the espresso machine and issues commands in two words: 'Firmer. Straighter.' Reception smells of freshly ground coffee, the phone rings, she ignores it with the authority of somebody who knows what matters.`,opts:[{t:`Cut it short and press the grinder button`,m:10,l:5,a:-5,b:0,r:`Gabi pushes your hand away like a child's at the cooker. 'That will get you nowhere.' You get a cappuccino regardless. Out of mercy. It tastes of mercy.`},{t:`Ask where she learned all this`,m:15,l:0,a:-10,b:0,r:`'Three years as a barista, before this.' Gabi wipes the group head down without looking. 'Sometimes it is only the machine I miss.' She says it lightly, and precisely for that reason the sentence stays with you all day.`},{t:`Listen, tamp, learn`,m:20,l:0,a:-15,b:0,r:`The third attempt runs dark and thick, the crema holds. Gabi tastes it and nods once. 'There you are, then.' You drink the finest coffee in your company history standing between the parcel desk and the doorbell panel, and from now on you have a standing offer here.`}]}];export{e as coffee};